WEBVTT

1
00:00:46.083 --> 00:00:51.625
PLANET: CHITON
POLITICAL REGIME: DICTATORSHIP

2
00:00:51.792 --> 00:00:57.292
LEADER: ADMIRAL SKORBA
POPULATION: 250,000

3
00:00:58.375 --> 00:01:01.458
POPULATION: 250,001

4
00:01:15.458 --> 00:01:17.542
Eureka, it worked!

5
00:01:18.667 --> 00:01:20.458
It worked!

6
00:01:20.625 --> 00:01:22.708
Oh, he's beautiful!

7
00:01:23.792 --> 00:01:25.667
He looks like a normal baby.

8
00:01:31.875 --> 00:01:33.500
It can't be them.

9
00:01:33.750 --> 00:01:36.583
They can't have found out so soon.

10
00:01:38.833 --> 00:01:41.833
- We have to hide him, Jan!
- They'll end up finding him.

11
00:01:42.042 --> 00:01:43.500
So...?

12
00:01:44.167 --> 00:01:45.417
There's only one thing we can do.

13
00:01:59.833 --> 00:02:01.000
They're here.

14
00:02:07.000 --> 00:02:09.458
- Good.
- You'll free us from them.

15
00:02:09.583 --> 00:02:10.792
Some day.

16
00:02:17.458 --> 00:02:20.458
You'll be safe here.
It's the planet's most advanced zone.

17
00:02:37.125 --> 00:02:40.167
When you grow up,
you'll come back to save us.

18
00:02:47.500 --> 00:02:50.917
- Get out of my labs, you rats!
- Go back to your sewers.

19
00:03:02.208 --> 00:03:05.375
First of all, good morning.

20
00:03:10.458 --> 00:03:12.583
I know everything.
Don't waste my time.

21
00:03:12.750 --> 00:03:16.833
- He's my son!
- No, he's an experiment.

22
00:03:17.292 --> 00:03:19.500
- Where did you put him?
- Where you can't find him.

23
00:03:19.625 --> 00:03:24.167
Don't make me push the button
and end this once and for all.

24
00:03:24.750 --> 00:03:25.875
I can help.

25
00:03:26.250 --> 00:03:29.083
I've no time for nonsense, Agata.

26
00:03:29.250 --> 00:03:32.042
But Dad, my cousin Sigfred
is the same age as me

27
00:03:32.208 --> 00:03:33.500
and they let him torture.

28
00:03:33.667 --> 00:03:35.792
Remember when I asked you

29
00:03:36.000 --> 00:03:39.042
to find all the pets on this planet
to annihilate them...

30
00:03:39.208 --> 00:03:41.250
...and you hid some of them?

31
00:03:41.417 --> 00:03:43.792
I felt sorry for them,
but I've changed, I'm matured.

32
00:03:44.000 --> 00:03:45.750
I don't get how you
can be my daughter.

33
00:03:45.917 --> 00:03:48.417
You always make me look foolish!

34
00:03:52.375 --> 00:03:53.833
It's...

35
00:03:54.042 --> 00:03:56.000
...a blue planet.

36
00:03:56.500 --> 00:03:58.583
Earth, Planet Earth.

37
00:04:00.542 --> 00:04:03.458
- Are you sure?
- Yes, I saw it. I know where it is.

38
00:04:03.583 --> 00:04:05.500
You can't do anything.
That boy will finish you off!

39
00:04:06.042 --> 00:04:09.333
Fine. You want me
to be proud of you?

40
00:04:09.917 --> 00:04:12.208
If you want to sit
on this throne one day,

41
00:04:13.167 --> 00:04:15.167
there's your chance.

42
00:04:20.500 --> 00:04:23.250
Listen to me, Agata.
That boy is the ultimate weapon.

43
00:04:23.417 --> 00:04:25.125
I want him alive.

44
00:04:25.500 --> 00:04:28.125
When you capture him,
I'll come for you.

45
00:04:28.292 --> 00:04:31.042
Yes, Dad.
It'll be soon, I won't let you down.

46
00:06:28.542 --> 00:06:30.333
LOPEZ GARAGE

47
00:06:35.375 --> 00:06:39.500
Here we go, the typical creep
on high beam from miles off.

48
00:06:39.625 --> 00:06:42.458
- Don't start, Juan. Let him pass.
- No, I will not.

49
00:06:42.583 --> 00:06:44.667
That hothead isn't overtaking me.

50
00:06:44.833 --> 00:06:47.292
And you'll ruin your timing belt!

51
00:06:47.458 --> 00:06:49.500
You clown!

52
00:07:03.000 --> 00:07:05.500
- Are you thinking what I'm thinking?
- Yes.

53
00:07:05.625 --> 00:07:07.250
What are you thinking?

54
00:07:07.417 --> 00:07:10.750
- I don't know right now. You?
- That wasn't a car.

55
00:07:23.542 --> 00:07:24.917
Jeez!

56
00:07:25.125 --> 00:07:28.708
I'll strip this heap
and make a pile on the parts!

57
00:07:28.875 --> 00:07:30.458
It's a meteorite, Juan.

58
00:07:30.583 --> 00:07:34.542
Or worse, an asteroid,
I don't really know the difference.

59
00:07:34.708 --> 00:07:37.000
Sorry, I'm getting nervous.

60
00:07:44.208 --> 00:07:45.792
Juan, I heard something.

61
00:07:46.000 --> 00:07:47.792
- Come here.
- You can hear something.

62
00:07:48.000 --> 00:07:51.458
- Maria, don't go near it.
- Someone's inside. Be quiet.

63
00:07:53.833 --> 00:07:56.292
Look, Juan! Look!

64
00:07:56.458 --> 00:08:00.042
- It's a gift from heaven.
- Like hell it's a gift!

65
00:08:00.875 --> 00:08:02.667
Look at the baby!

66
00:08:02.833 --> 00:08:04.375
We'll keep it.

67
00:08:04.500 --> 00:08:06.500
We can't, he's not ours!

68
00:08:06.667 --> 00:08:09.333
But look at him, he's lovely.

69
00:08:16.083 --> 00:08:19.125
Honey, that's no baby,
it's an adult dwarf.

70
00:08:20.375 --> 00:08:24.458
- We can't leave him here.
- That mustache is weird.

71
00:08:24.583 --> 00:08:27.750
- What do we know about kids?
- I know they don't fall from the sky.

72
00:08:27.917 --> 00:08:29.417
If it's a miracle, they do.

73
00:08:29.542 --> 00:08:32.000
I've been praying for months
for us to have a child.

74
00:08:32.792 --> 00:08:35.583
Maria, you're crazy.

75
00:08:36.917 --> 00:08:38.625
Hi, Daddy!

76
00:08:38.792 --> 00:08:40.750
Hi, Daddy!

77
00:08:40.917 --> 00:08:43.458
Look, Daddy.

78
00:08:43.875 --> 00:08:45.625
Look, little guy.

79
00:08:45.792 --> 00:08:47.708
He knows who his dad is.

80
00:08:50.167 --> 00:08:51.500
Little guy!

81
00:09:29.875 --> 00:09:34.000
Well, apart from the mustache,
he looks normal to me.

82
00:09:43.250 --> 00:09:44.417
- Good morning.
- Good morning.

83
00:09:44.542 --> 00:09:46.458
- My car's running wonky.
- Don't worry, my friend.

84
00:09:46.583 --> 00:09:50.000
We'll leave it like new,
we have the latest technology.

85
00:09:51.917 --> 00:09:53.875
I prefer more conventional
methods, thanks.

86
00:10:23.333 --> 00:10:25.500
Lopez! Push harder!

87
00:10:25.625 --> 00:10:29.417
You're a weakling!
Go, shithead! Harder!

88
00:10:29.542 --> 00:10:31.583
Wuss! Piece of shit!

89
00:10:47.417 --> 00:10:48.833
- Come on, here!
- Here!

90
00:10:49.042 --> 00:10:51.125
- Pass it to me!
- Kick it already!

91
00:10:51.292 --> 00:10:53.417
- You loser, kick it!
- Numbskull goalie!

92
00:10:53.542 --> 00:10:56.083
C'mon, mustache!

93
00:10:56.250 --> 00:10:59.042
Pass it, kid! Loser!

94
00:11:01.167 --> 00:11:02.458
Doofus!

95
00:11:02.583 --> 00:11:04.500
Pass it, you idiot!

96
00:11:19.708 --> 00:11:22.042
Goal!

97
00:11:23.125 --> 00:11:24.208
Hit me!

98
00:11:24.875 --> 00:11:27.625
- Goal!
- No way.

99
00:11:27.792 --> 00:11:29.417
I got a goal. What's wrong?

100
00:11:30.292 --> 00:11:31.583
Let's go!

101
00:11:32.458 --> 00:11:33.500
What's wrong?

102
00:11:35.417 --> 00:11:36.542
Ball hog.

103
00:11:38.042 --> 00:11:40.667
I told you not to do those things
in front of people.

104
00:11:40.833 --> 00:11:41.833
But I want to win!

105
00:11:42.042 --> 00:11:44.083
All you'll get is no one
wanting to play with you.

106
00:11:44.250 --> 00:11:45.667
That's the way of a cheat.

107
00:11:45.833 --> 00:11:47.625
A coward who won't play right.

108
00:11:47.792 --> 00:11:50.833
- It's how I play. That's me.
- Then hide it, son, hide it.

109
00:11:51.042 --> 00:11:53.500
Keep going and they'll think
you're a weirdo

110
00:11:53.625 --> 00:11:55.583
and you'll be lonelier
than the number one.

111
00:12:26.708 --> 00:12:28.667
Maybe you didn't tell them
the right time.

112
00:12:29.417 --> 00:12:32.000
- Are you sure you did?
- Sure I did.

113
00:12:32.167 --> 00:12:34.042
And the address?
Did you give them the address?

114
00:12:34.208 --> 00:12:37.292
- Is it on the invite?
- They didn't want to come, Dad.

115
00:12:37.458 --> 00:12:39.583
It's because I do weird stuff, huh?

116
00:12:39.750 --> 00:12:42.500
Not weird, honey, just special.

117
00:12:42.667 --> 00:12:44.875
Then why is it bad?

118
00:12:45.083 --> 00:12:46.667
Because you're in Spain.

119
00:12:46.833 --> 00:12:48.167
Look, son. Anywhere else,

120
00:12:48.333 --> 00:12:51.875
in Germany, France, Norway,
you'd be highly prized.

121
00:12:52.625 --> 00:12:55.375
The bad thing is that here,
tall poppies get cut down.

122
00:12:55.500 --> 00:12:56.917
If you stand out,
they grind you down.

123
00:12:57.125 --> 00:12:59.167
Is that why my classmates didn't come?

124
00:12:59.333 --> 00:13:02.625
- Because I'm not like them?
- They'll never be like you.

125
00:13:02.792 --> 00:13:06.042
But if you don't do "your stuff",
you can be like them.

126
00:13:06.375 --> 00:13:09.125
Juanito, you don't need to
do anything special,

127
00:13:09.292 --> 00:13:11.458
nothing special, to go far.

128
00:13:11.583 --> 00:13:15.500
Listen, in this country, to be happy
you have to be mediocre.

129
00:13:15.792 --> 00:13:17.667
Come on, son, make a wish.

130
00:13:18.750 --> 00:13:20.042
To be normal.

131
00:13:24.208 --> 00:13:27.042
Juanito, next year
I'm making you a cupcake.

132
00:13:30.458 --> 00:13:33.833
20 YEARS LATER

133
00:13:35.333 --> 00:13:38.708
<i>...the best electrical appliances
at the best prices.</i>

134
00:13:39.000 --> 00:13:40.083
<i>Take the step.</i>

135
00:13:40.667 --> 00:13:43.833
<i>Naturally, with the guarantee
of Chip Technologies.</i>

136
00:13:49.083 --> 00:13:50.083
Yes?

137
00:13:51.375 --> 00:13:53.292
- Where are you?
- Uh... here.

138
00:13:53.458 --> 00:13:55.917
- Where? Did you sleep in again?
- No, no.

139
00:13:56.125 --> 00:13:58.917
In the office, doing the dispatches.

140
00:13:59.125 --> 00:14:02.875
- I went by before and didn't see you.
- I must've been in the bathroom.

141
00:14:03.083 --> 00:14:04.417
- <i>After, when?</i>
- A while ago.

142
00:14:04.542 --> 00:14:06.583
Yes, a while ago...

143
00:14:06.750 --> 00:14:07.750
I was in the bathroom.

144
00:14:08.708 --> 00:14:10.250
I'm coming to see you,
to tell you something.

145
00:14:10.417 --> 00:14:11.375
<i>- Okay?</i>
- No, really,...

146
00:14:11.500 --> 00:14:13.000
I'm tied up with the reports.

147
00:14:13.167 --> 00:14:16.208
- Wasn't it the dispatches?
- The ones that don't match the reports.

148
00:14:19.875 --> 00:14:20.542
Darn it.

149
00:14:46.375 --> 00:14:48.333
- Have you seen Lopez?
- No, I haven't.

150
00:14:48.500 --> 00:14:49.667
Neither have I.

151
00:14:55.625 --> 00:14:58.833
- You could've warned me, eh?
- Look out for the box!

152
00:15:11.667 --> 00:15:13.875
- When did you get here?
- I don't know.

153
00:15:14.083 --> 00:15:16.125
I came in early today,
I'm so busy.

154
00:15:16.292 --> 00:15:19.042
Juan, you know I don't want you
to see me as a boss.

155
00:15:19.208 --> 00:15:21.000
You and I are friends
above everything.

156
00:15:21.167 --> 00:15:23.583
- Does something smell weird?
- You're the weird one.

157
00:15:23.750 --> 00:15:26.000
It's cologne, expensive too.

158
00:15:26.167 --> 00:15:27.500
Since when do you use cologne?

159
00:15:27.667 --> 00:15:29.167
To discuss that,
I'll take off my boss hat

160
00:15:29.333 --> 00:15:32.500
and put on my friend hat.
Work and friendship can't mix.

161
00:15:32.667 --> 00:15:34.917
Technically, you're not my boss.

162
00:15:36.042 --> 00:15:38.375
She's starting today,
I hired her after all.

163
00:15:38.500 --> 00:15:40.875
- You got that girl the job?
- It's not like that.

164
00:15:41.083 --> 00:15:42.708
She deserved the job.

165
00:15:42.917 --> 00:15:46.250
Another thing is if something
came up in the interviews,

166
00:15:46.417 --> 00:15:47.708
a spark, you might say.

167
00:15:47.875 --> 00:15:49.583
You can't use interviews to score.

168
00:15:49.750 --> 00:15:52.625
Everyone knows that job interviews
are a bit like dates.

169
00:15:52.792 --> 00:15:54.333
No, they're not.

170
00:15:54.500 --> 00:15:58.208
On a date, what do you
talk about? Work, hobbies...

171
00:15:58.375 --> 00:16:00.500
Speaking of hobbies,

172
00:16:00.625 --> 00:16:03.833
you won't believe it, but ours
are the same: reading and travel.

173
00:16:04.042 --> 00:16:05.333
But everyone likes that!

174
00:16:05.500 --> 00:16:08.792
Help me plan something cool,
as a welcome.

175
00:16:09.000 --> 00:16:10.417
We've never welcomed anyone.

176
00:16:10.542 --> 00:16:12.875
I'm putting on my friend hat
to tell you

177
00:16:13.083 --> 00:16:15.292
that you and I haven't
been out partying in ages.

178
00:16:15.458 --> 00:16:17.875
Count me out.
I'm getting breakfast.

179
00:16:18.833 --> 00:16:20.792
I knew it. You just got here!

180
00:16:24.333 --> 00:16:25.458
Darn it.

181
00:16:50.000 --> 00:16:50.750
Luisa?

182
00:17:03.125 --> 00:17:05.292
Good morning. Can you tell...

183
00:17:05.458 --> 00:17:06.917
No... Juan?

184
00:17:07.625 --> 00:17:09.625
- Luisa?
- What are you doing here?

185
00:17:10.417 --> 00:17:13.208
I knew in college that
you'd go far and look at you,

186
00:17:13.375 --> 00:17:14.333
a receptionist.

187
00:17:14.792 --> 00:17:17.583
No, I don't work here.

188
00:17:17.750 --> 00:17:20.125
I work in the company,
but in a real job.

189
00:17:21.292 --> 00:17:24.292
- Okay, you're kidding me.
- Amazing meeting like this!

190
00:17:24.458 --> 00:17:26.792
We must catch up.
But not now, I'm late.

191
00:17:27.000 --> 00:17:29.583
- Could you tell Jaime Gonzalez?
- Jaime?

192
00:17:29.750 --> 00:17:33.000
- You're going to work here?
- Looks like it. I still can't believe it.

193
00:17:33.167 --> 00:17:34.708
Did you have to do
8 interviews too?

194
00:17:39.083 --> 00:17:40.375
- Jaime.
- <i>Yes?</i>

195
00:17:40.500 --> 00:17:42.500
- Luis Lanas is here.
- <i>Send her in.</i>

196
00:17:42.667 --> 00:17:43.708
Okay.

197
00:17:44.667 --> 00:17:46.208
You're great at it.

198
00:17:46.375 --> 00:17:48.917
You should seriously consider
being a receptionist.

199
00:17:53.375 --> 00:17:55.208
Normally with new people

200
00:17:55.375 --> 00:17:57.708
we have a welcoming party.

201
00:17:57.875 --> 00:18:01.000
A little drink.
Are you into that?

202
00:18:02.375 --> 00:18:05.083
Right, family, look out,
we're making an auto-selfie.

203
00:18:05.250 --> 00:18:07.667
I know it's not a selfie,
strictly speaking,

204
00:18:07.833 --> 00:18:10.083
but you get my drift.

205
00:18:13.083 --> 00:18:15.000
A nice memento of you first day,
right, Luisa?

206
00:18:15.167 --> 00:18:17.667
That's what we're like here.
A great atmosphere.

207
00:18:17.833 --> 00:18:19.542
Going out and living it up
any day of the week.

208
00:18:19.708 --> 00:18:22.417
- Where's the bathroom?
- Through the door, on the right.

209
00:18:26.250 --> 00:18:28.500
- How do you know her?
- From college.

210
00:18:28.667 --> 00:18:30.750
- She was a friend's girlfriend.
- Did you like her?

211
00:18:30.917 --> 00:18:33.625
He wasn't a close friend...

212
00:18:33.792 --> 00:18:36.542
- I asked if you liked her.
- Jaime, no. I didn't.

213
00:18:36.708 --> 00:18:39.833
Sir, if there's nothing else,
we'll get going too.

214
00:18:40.500 --> 00:18:43.000
Stay here until I tell you, okay?

215
00:18:43.167 --> 00:18:45.667
Our shift ended two hours ago.

216
00:18:45.833 --> 00:18:47.833
Look. See that gadget?

217
00:18:48.333 --> 00:18:51.083
It's got more commitment
to the company than both of you.

218
00:18:53.042 --> 00:18:55.042
I always need my boss hat
with those two.

219
00:18:55.208 --> 00:18:58.375
We've had a drink.
That's enough, isn't it?

220
00:18:59.250 --> 00:19:02.500
If you all go at once,
she'll get suspicious.

221
00:19:02.667 --> 00:19:04.917
I want to order a pizza
with lots of black olives.

222
00:19:05.125 --> 00:19:06.250
She loves black olives.

223
00:19:06.417 --> 00:19:08.500
You asked in the interview
how she like her pizzas?

224
00:19:08.667 --> 00:19:11.542
When she comes back,
go to the corner shop for ice

225
00:19:11.708 --> 00:19:12.500
and don't come back.

226
00:19:12.667 --> 00:19:16.042
You know what that's called?
Strategy.

227
00:19:16.208 --> 00:19:18.042
<i>The H.R. guy's coming on to me.</i>

228
00:19:18.208 --> 00:19:20.333
<i>I told you he was already
in the interviews.</i>

229
00:19:21.083 --> 00:19:23.458
<i>I'll make some excuse and go.</i>

230
00:19:23.583 --> 00:19:26.833
<i>No, wait.
Remember Juan, from college?</i>

231
00:19:27.042 --> 00:19:28.875
<i>That's him, with the mustache.</i>

232
00:19:29.083 --> 00:19:30.542
<i>He works here too.</i>

233
00:19:31.292 --> 00:19:32.375
<i>Just as well he's at the party.</i>

234
00:19:36.000 --> 00:19:37.500
- Juan!
- What?

235
00:19:37.667 --> 00:19:40.917
- Yes, I'll stick around.
- Stick around?

236
00:19:42.833 --> 00:19:45.167
Juanito, go get some ice.

237
00:19:45.458 --> 00:19:48.375
We've been knocking it back so much
we run out of ice.

238
00:19:48.500 --> 00:19:49.500
Yes, there's ice.

239
00:19:50.333 --> 00:19:52.917
- No, there's no ice.
- Yes.

240
00:19:53.500 --> 00:19:54.208
Where?

241
00:20:08.875 --> 00:20:09.875
Ice.

242
00:20:14.042 --> 00:20:15.042
Where's Luisa?

243
00:20:15.875 --> 00:20:19.292
I don't want to brag,
but I think she got scared.

244
00:20:20.208 --> 00:20:23.083
The tension here was too much
for her and she chose to go.

245
00:20:23.542 --> 00:20:26.292
A shame, because I was already
thinking about my Aunt Clari.

246
00:20:26.458 --> 00:20:29.000
Don't give them that crap
about your Aunt Clari.

247
00:20:29.167 --> 00:20:32.292
Juan, they have a right
to know too. Don't be racist.

248
00:20:32.583 --> 00:20:35.833
A trick to keep going in bed,
and I don't mean sleeping.

249
00:20:36.292 --> 00:20:37.375
I think of three images:

250
00:20:37.500 --> 00:20:39.792
my Aunt Clari dancing,

251
00:20:40.000 --> 00:20:43.000
a leek pie
and beige corduroy pants.

252
00:20:43.167 --> 00:20:44.083
Okay, got it?

253
00:20:44.250 --> 00:20:46.708
I go from one to another
in my head. One...

254
00:20:47.292 --> 00:20:48.250
...the other...

255
00:20:49.125 --> 00:20:50.250
...the other.

256
00:20:50.417 --> 00:20:52.625
That way I can spend
hours with a woman.

257
00:20:52.792 --> 00:20:55.917
Well, not hours, what a chore.

258
00:21:16.792 --> 00:21:18.417
Psst, Juan!

259
00:21:19.792 --> 00:21:20.708
What are you doing?

260
00:21:22.000 --> 00:21:24.792
- I was on my way home.
- Straight home or out?

261
00:21:26.292 --> 00:21:28.333
I don't know. Are you hungry?

262
00:21:29.167 --> 00:21:29.875
You?

263
00:21:31.458 --> 00:21:32.333
Pizza?

264
00:21:36.500 --> 00:21:37.500
Well, next time.

265
00:21:38.125 --> 00:21:40.292
- Hey, maybe I'll make it.
- You'll make it...

266
00:21:40.458 --> 00:21:44.083
- I will. What do you bet?
- You won't. See you tomorrow.

267
00:21:54.000 --> 00:21:55.250
Excuse me.

268
00:21:56.583 --> 00:21:58.583
Do you like black olives?

269
00:22:00.833 --> 00:22:03.292
- How's Rober?
- What Rober?

270
00:22:03.917 --> 00:22:07.083
- What other Rober would there be?
- From college?

271
00:22:07.250 --> 00:22:09.458
- Yes. Are you still together?
- Juan, please.

272
00:22:09.583 --> 00:22:11.250
We left college 10 years ago.

273
00:22:11.417 --> 00:22:13.792
We weren't even an item.
How could I be with Rober?

274
00:22:14.000 --> 00:22:16.125
I don't know, just asking.

275
00:22:16.292 --> 00:22:19.000
If he found out I was here
eating with you, he'd freak.

276
00:22:19.167 --> 00:22:22.833
- Freak? Why?
- Rober always, I don't know,

277
00:22:23.083 --> 00:22:26.083
- thought you were weird.
- People talk too much.

278
00:22:26.250 --> 00:22:28.792
He'd say: "Don't you think
he's hiding something?".

279
00:22:29.000 --> 00:22:32.292
I'd say: "Juan seems
really normal to me".

280
00:22:32.792 --> 00:22:34.417
That's what I say.

281
00:22:35.292 --> 00:22:37.500
What do I have to hide?

282
00:22:39.833 --> 00:22:41.625
You wanted to know
if I have a boyfriend.

283
00:22:51.625 --> 00:22:55.292
- Let's go somewhere else, eh?
- We'll finish this and go.

284
00:22:57.792 --> 00:22:59.750
Will you keep it down?!

285
00:23:01.750 --> 00:23:03.792
- What are you laughing at?
- Luisa...

286
00:23:04.208 --> 00:23:05.500
You, squirt.

287
00:23:06.292 --> 00:23:08.833
- What's so funny?
- Shut up, you old bat.

288
00:23:09.042 --> 00:23:11.333
Don't get mad, Luisa.

289
00:23:15.417 --> 00:23:16.333
What did you say?

290
00:23:16.500 --> 00:23:19.167
Luisa, we can finish up...

291
00:23:19.333 --> 00:23:22.208
- You gonna be the hero, or what?
- Me, no. I didn't say a thing.

292
00:23:22.375 --> 00:23:24.417
Maybe we'll bust your ass.

293
00:23:24.542 --> 00:23:26.375
- You, bust my ass?
- I didn't say it, it was her.

294
00:23:26.500 --> 00:23:29.500
- What if he does?
- It's illegal to hit a minor.

295
00:23:29.833 --> 00:23:32.042
- I'm 18. What's up?
- Jeez.

296
00:23:32.208 --> 00:23:34.667
It's illegal to hit people in general.

297
00:23:34.833 --> 00:23:36.500
See this finger?

298
00:23:36.625 --> 00:23:39.167
- I'll blow you down with my index finger.
- Two things.

299
00:23:39.333 --> 00:23:42.000
One, that's not your index finger,
it's your middle finger.

300
00:23:42.167 --> 00:23:44.042
And two, beyond that detail,

301
00:23:44.208 --> 00:23:46.042
you can't floor me

302
00:23:46.208 --> 00:23:48.333
with that finger
or anything else.

303
00:23:53.833 --> 00:23:55.208
Here, the middle finger.

304
00:23:56.458 --> 00:23:57.583
<i>Loser!</i>

305
00:24:08.250 --> 00:24:10.792
<i>My son, remember these words,</i>

306
00:24:11.000 --> 00:24:13.042
<i>if you stand out,
they'll grind you down.</i>

307
00:24:13.208 --> 00:24:16.208
<i>Tall poppies get cut down.</i>

308
00:24:16.375 --> 00:24:20.167
<i>Juanito, you don't need to
do anything special to go far.</i>

309
00:24:20.333 --> 00:24:22.167
<i>Don't get involved.</i>

310
00:24:22.333 --> 00:24:25.542
<i>No one gave you
any cards in this game.</i>

311
00:24:26.792 --> 00:24:29.875
FINAL DESTINATION
NEXT TRAIN:

312
00:24:40.500 --> 00:24:42.667
<i>107 to Central, please!</i>

313
00:24:42.833 --> 00:24:44.667
<i>107 to Central!</i>

314
00:24:44.833 --> 00:24:46.375
<i>Help, please!</i>

315
00:24:46.500 --> 00:24:48.625
<i>The breaks aren't responding!</i>

316
00:24:48.792 --> 00:24:50.625
<i>We're a runaway!</i>

317
00:24:51.333 --> 00:24:54.750
<i>107 to Central!
The brakes aren't responding!</i>

318
00:24:54.917 --> 00:24:56.750
<i>We're going to crash!</i>

319
00:25:07.333 --> 00:25:09.625
What was that?

320
00:25:10.583 --> 00:25:12.542
IT'S TIME, TAKE THE STEP

321
00:25:15.333 --> 00:25:17.542
IT'S TIME, TAKE THE STEP

322
00:25:57.458 --> 00:26:00.167
Relax. It's all under control.

323
00:26:27.667 --> 00:26:28.792
What are you doing?

324
00:26:29.667 --> 00:26:31.167
I don't known!

325
00:28:40.208 --> 00:28:41.708
CHIT TECHNOLOGIES
WORLD HQ

326
00:28:41.875 --> 00:28:46.917
You're about to witness the birth
of a new technological revolution.

327
00:28:47.917 --> 00:28:52.042
I present a future member
of our family:

328
00:28:52.500 --> 00:28:53.667
Chitobot.

329
00:28:55.250 --> 00:28:58.333
Your homes will never be
the same again.

330
00:28:58.500 --> 00:29:01.875
Ultimate cleaning:
it vacuums, sweeps and mops.

331
00:29:02.083 --> 00:29:06.208
Of course, with the
technical service of CHIT.

332
00:29:07.042 --> 00:29:08.708
It's time to take the step.

333
00:29:16.792 --> 00:29:17.792
Agata...

334
00:29:22.000 --> 00:29:23.000
We've found him.

335
00:29:23.167 --> 00:29:24.583
Are you sure?

336
00:29:24.750 --> 00:29:26.375
Someone stopped
a subway train in Spain.

337
00:29:35.417 --> 00:29:36.667
Hit the video!

338
00:29:39.417 --> 00:29:40.417
What video?

339
00:29:41.500 --> 00:29:44.000
Spain? What's someone like that
doing in Spain?

340
00:29:44.167 --> 00:29:46.250
Last he stopped
one of our derailments.

341
00:29:46.417 --> 00:29:48.708
Did some idiot hit
the emergency brake?

342
00:29:48.875 --> 00:29:51.708
No, we always deactivate them
before causing an accident.

343
00:29:51.875 --> 00:29:53.458
We have the images
in the control room.

344
00:29:53.583 --> 00:29:54.667
I don't need them.

345
00:30:04.292 --> 00:30:05.542
None of them show his face?

346
00:30:05.708 --> 00:30:07.833
The whole planet is full
of our technology.

347
00:30:08.042 --> 00:30:10.292
- He has no way out.
- There's no time to lose.

348
00:30:10.458 --> 00:30:13.000
Warn my clones there
that I'm coming immediately.

349
00:30:13.167 --> 00:30:15.000
And stay alert.

350
00:30:15.500 --> 00:30:19.375
Remember, we're facing
the ultimate weapon.

351
00:30:21.500 --> 00:30:23.542
Coffee with cream and a croissant.

352
00:30:24.833 --> 00:30:27.625
The coffee and pastry no,
but I can cream you.

353
00:30:27.792 --> 00:30:30.208
Warm or hot?

354
00:30:31.375 --> 00:30:32.833
Sorry, sir.

355
00:30:38.042 --> 00:30:41.167
SUPERHERO?

356
00:30:41.333 --> 00:30:44.458
<i>Everyone's talking about
the strange subway event yesterday.</i>

357
00:30:44.583 --> 00:30:46.167
<i>An unknown man
leapt onto the tracks</i>

358
00:30:46.333 --> 00:30:48.708
<i>causing chaos and astonishment
among those present.</i>

359
00:30:48.875 --> 00:30:52.333
<i>We have exclusive images
from the security cameras...</i>

360
00:30:52.500 --> 00:30:55.208
He's got a comet on his back.
You can't go that fast!

361
00:30:55.417 --> 00:30:57.208
Let's do a bit of work, right?

362
00:30:57.375 --> 00:30:59.583
We get sidetracked by anything here.

363
00:30:59.750 --> 00:31:02.917
- You're right, it's no big deal.
- I didn't say that either.

364
00:31:03.125 --> 00:31:05.167
You stop a speeding subway train...

365
00:31:05.333 --> 00:31:07.833
- What?
- Explain last night, right now.

366
00:31:08.042 --> 00:31:09.917
- What happened last night?
- Don't pretend with me!

367
00:31:10.125 --> 00:31:12.417
- I didn't stop a train!
- What train?

368
00:31:12.542 --> 00:31:15.125
- What train?
- I'm talking about Jaime.

369
00:31:15.792 --> 00:31:17.792
- His weird party last night.
- Oh, okay.

370
00:31:18.000 --> 00:31:20.625
Look what he gave me today.
My personal cards.

371
00:31:20.792 --> 00:31:22.292
500 of them.

372
00:31:22.458 --> 00:31:23.917
I don't want to be dirty minded,

373
00:31:24.125 --> 00:31:25.792
but it's like he hired me
to hit on me.

374
00:31:27.208 --> 00:31:30.125
Luisa, that's the way Jaime is.

375
00:31:30.292 --> 00:31:32.375
- What are you all looking at?
- It's nothing.

376
00:31:32.500 --> 00:31:34.083
- Let me see.
- It's nothing!

377
00:31:34.250 --> 00:31:35.333
- What is it?
- Luisa, it's nothing.

378
00:31:36.333 --> 00:31:38.208
Oh, that crap.

379
00:31:38.375 --> 00:31:41.083
You can see a mile off
that it's a publicity stunt.

380
00:31:41.250 --> 00:31:44.083
A guy with superpowers in Spain?

381
00:31:44.250 --> 00:31:45.458
Shut up, it's pathetic.

382
00:31:47.042 --> 00:31:48.833
- Not really pathetic, eh?
- Juan...

383
00:31:49.042 --> 00:31:52.500
A superhero turns up and he's Spanish,
the crappiest you can get.

384
00:31:52.667 --> 00:31:56.500
A superhero has to be American,
or English or Japanese.

385
00:31:56.625 --> 00:31:58.500
What, was he born
in Arguijuela de Todos los Santos,

386
00:31:58.667 --> 00:32:00.167
Province of Caceres? No, Juan.

387
00:32:00.333 --> 00:32:01.542
Luisa...

388
00:32:01.708 --> 00:32:03.292
...imagine, not you and me, no,

389
00:32:03.458 --> 00:32:06.333
but if there were someone
totally altruistic,

390
00:32:06.500 --> 00:32:09.875
capable of risking his life
to save the lives of lots of people...

391
00:32:10.083 --> 00:32:13.292
No, Juan. Some things don't fit.
Superhero and Spanish, no.

392
00:32:13.458 --> 00:32:15.667
German, maybe.
He could be German.

393
00:32:15.833 --> 00:32:17.375
But Spanish?
Don't make me laugh.

394
00:32:17.500 --> 00:32:19.042
Who's the villain: Punctuality?

395
00:32:20.542 --> 00:32:23.125
Maybe he's not a superhero.

396
00:32:23.292 --> 00:32:26.125
- Maybe he's someone special.
- You're irritating today.

397
00:32:26.292 --> 00:32:28.292
Keep it up, and I won't
have dinner with you tonight.

398
00:32:28.917 --> 00:32:30.542
- Dinner, the two of us?
- What's wrong?

399
00:32:30.708 --> 00:32:34.750
- What are you talking about?
- Nothing, work.

400
00:32:34.917 --> 00:32:37.292
Then you haven't found out.

401
00:32:37.750 --> 00:32:40.250
Agata Muller has come to Spain.

402
00:32:41.208 --> 00:32:42.667
The vacuum cleaner lady?

403
00:32:42.833 --> 00:32:45.917
Well, the technological guru,
I like to call her.

404
00:32:46.125 --> 00:32:49.208
But yes, basically
she sells vacuum cleaners.

405
00:32:49.542 --> 00:32:51.125
You look nice today, Luisa.

406
00:32:51.292 --> 00:32:53.667
<i>News of the day is about
the visit to our country</i>

407
00:32:53.833 --> 00:32:57.083
<i>of possibly the world's
most famous businesswoman.</i>

408
00:32:57.458 --> 00:33:00.750
<i>Our people are already with
the multimillionaire Agata Muller,</i>

409
00:33:00.917 --> 00:33:03.250
<i>who's about to make a statement.</i>

410
00:33:03.417 --> 00:33:04.500
<i>We go live.</i>

411
00:33:04.625 --> 00:33:06.375
<i>I've always wanted to meet
someone like this.</i>

412
00:33:06.500 --> 00:33:09.292
<i>We're used to pursuing
those who commit crimes.</i>

413
00:33:09.458 --> 00:33:11.292
<i>It's also important to find</i>

414
00:33:11.458 --> 00:33:13.500
<i>those who stand out
for doing things right.</i>

415
00:33:13.667 --> 00:33:15.917
<i>So I wish to send him this message.</i>

416
00:33:16.125 --> 00:33:17.917
<i>I know that he's listening.</i>

417
00:33:18.833 --> 00:33:20.292
<i>Whoever you are,</i>

418
00:33:20.458 --> 00:33:22.083
<i>I want you to know
that I've come to help you</i>

419
00:33:22.250 --> 00:33:24.917
<i>and thank you for being that hero.</i>

420
00:33:25.125 --> 00:33:29.500
<i>And to tell you that you and I
can do great things together.</i>

421
00:33:29.625 --> 00:33:31.875
Like I said, publicity.

422
00:33:34.083 --> 00:33:36.667
CHIT TECHNOLOGIES
BARCELONA OFFICE

423
00:33:36.833 --> 00:33:38.833
It's time to go home.

424
00:33:39.250 --> 00:33:41.417
It's time to go home.

425
00:33:47.417 --> 00:33:48.625
It's time to go home.

426
00:33:48.792 --> 00:33:52.792
- <i>First of all, good morning.</i>
- Dad, it's me, Agata.

427
00:33:53.000 --> 00:33:55.417
<i>Yeah, great. What do you want?</i>

428
00:33:56.333 --> 00:33:58.625
Jan's son,
I've found him at last.

429
00:33:59.250 --> 00:34:01.750
<i>I didn't even think
you were still looking.</i>

430
00:34:01.917 --> 00:34:04.250
I told you I wouldn't let you down.

431
00:34:04.417 --> 00:34:07.542
<i>Yes, but it's been 30 years.
Don't expect me to applaud.</i>

432
00:34:08.333 --> 00:34:11.042
If you knew all the things
I've had to do...

433
00:34:11.208 --> 00:34:12.875
But now you can come and get me.

434
00:34:13.083 --> 00:34:16.250
- <i>Have you found him or got him?</i>
- I'm very close.

435
00:34:16.417 --> 00:34:18.917
He has no way out.
Only the easy part's left.

436
00:34:19.125 --> 00:34:21.500
- <i>Another 20 years?</i>
- When you find out what I've done,

437
00:34:21.625 --> 00:34:23.000
you'll be so proud of me.

438
00:34:23.167 --> 00:34:26.167
My technology has spread
to every corner of the planet

439
00:34:26.333 --> 00:34:27.583
and it controls everything.

440
00:34:27.750 --> 00:34:31.500
<i>Anyone else would've razed the planet
and been back in two days.</i>

441
00:34:31.667 --> 00:34:34.167
You said you wanted him alive.

442
00:34:34.333 --> 00:34:37.250
Come for me and we'll
raze the planet together.

443
00:34:37.417 --> 00:34:40.292
<i>If you don't have him
when I arrive, I will raze it...</i>

444
00:34:40.458 --> 00:34:42.083
<i>with you on it.</i>

445
00:34:51.000 --> 00:34:53.125
Gentleman, you have the big prize.

446
00:34:53.292 --> 00:34:55.042
So get on it immediately.

447
00:34:55.208 --> 00:34:56.458
Sure, boss.

448
00:34:56.583 --> 00:34:59.750
Still, we'll have to stop
the search the day after tomorrow,

449
00:34:59.917 --> 00:35:02.208
it's the patron saint's day festival.

450
00:35:04.500 --> 00:35:06.083
I'm the only patron here.

451
00:35:06.250 --> 00:35:09.333
And no one's stopping
until we trap Jan's son.

452
00:35:09.500 --> 00:35:10.625
- Understood?
- Yes.

453
00:35:16.042 --> 00:35:19.208
- Hi, Luisa. You're there already?
- Yes, half an hour ago.

454
00:35:19.375 --> 00:35:21.292
- I knew it.
- I'm on the bus.

455
00:35:21.458 --> 00:35:23.167
I'm 3, 4 minutes away.

456
00:35:23.333 --> 00:35:25.917
- For being late, you're buying.
- Okay.

457
00:35:31.667 --> 00:35:33.500
Relax, Dumbass. It's alright.

458
00:35:39.167 --> 00:35:42.167
<i>Jan's son, only you can hear me.</i>

459
00:35:42.333 --> 00:35:44.500
Please, can you turn the radio down?

460
00:35:44.667 --> 00:35:47.042
Radio? I don't have a radio.

461
00:35:50.458 --> 00:35:53.500
<i>If you can hear this,
you're who I'm looking for.</i>

462
00:35:53.667 --> 00:35:54.667
Who are you?

463
00:35:56.042 --> 00:35:58.333
- Me? I'm Pedro Luis.
- Don't get involved.

464
00:35:58.500 --> 00:35:59.583
Can't you see the state he's in?

465
00:35:59.750 --> 00:36:02.125
<i>Don't be scared. I'm your friend.</i>

466
00:36:02.292 --> 00:36:05.250
Please, could you stop the bus?
I need to get off here.

467
00:36:06.167 --> 00:36:08.042
Please, you're scaring the dog.

468
00:36:08.208 --> 00:36:09.292
Can't you see?!

469
00:36:09.708 --> 00:36:11.625
Driver, let him off, he's crazy!

470
00:36:11.792 --> 00:36:13.458
<i>I have to tell you two things.</i>

471
00:36:13.583 --> 00:36:16.625
God, turn it down,
my head's going to explode!

472
00:36:16.792 --> 00:36:20.458
<i>First, don't talk to me,
I can't hear you.</i>

473
00:36:24.583 --> 00:36:25.792
Oh, forget it, forget it.

474
00:36:26.542 --> 00:36:29.500
<i>Second, you have to
come see me.</i>

475
00:36:31.917 --> 00:36:33.583
<i>I am Agata Muller.</i>

476
00:36:34.583 --> 00:36:36.375
<i>Let's talk face to face.</i>

477
00:36:37.208 --> 00:36:39.708
<i>With your super-hearing
it'll be easy for you</i>

478
00:36:39.875 --> 00:36:42.125
<i>to detect the origin of my voice.</i>

479
00:36:42.292 --> 00:36:44.583
<i>You must have many questions.
But relax,</i>

480
00:36:44.750 --> 00:36:48.500
- <i>I'm here to explain everything.</i>
- Just shut up!

481
00:36:48.625 --> 00:36:51.750
<i>I don't get why it took you
so many years to take the step.</i>

482
00:36:51.917 --> 00:36:53.250
Yes, I'm coming!

483
00:36:53.417 --> 00:36:54.542
<i>You have nothing to fear.</i>

484
00:36:54.708 --> 00:36:57.417
<i>I know your secret
and I've come to help you.</i>

485
00:36:58.875 --> 00:37:01.250
<i>Welcome to Chit Technologies.</i>

486
00:37:04.458 --> 00:37:06.208
We were expecting you.

487
00:37:23.500 --> 00:37:24.792
Hello?

488
00:37:26.833 --> 00:37:29.250
Sorry, but I'm in kind of a hurry.

489
00:37:32.167 --> 00:37:34.583
You don't know how many years
I've waited for this moment.

490
00:37:36.000 --> 00:37:38.875
- You're the vacuum lady.
- 30 years.

491
00:37:39.083 --> 00:37:40.708
A whole life hoping to find you.

492
00:37:40.875 --> 00:37:43.500
Sit down, please.
We have a lot to celebrate.

493
00:37:43.667 --> 00:37:46.208
What do we have to celebrate?
I don't know you at all.

494
00:37:46.375 --> 00:37:49.458
Well, I know you from the TV,
I've got one of your blenders.

495
00:37:49.583 --> 00:37:52.125
What you did in the subway
the other night was spectacular.

496
00:37:52.458 --> 00:37:53.583
Stop, stop...

497
00:37:53.750 --> 00:37:55.583
I had absolutely nothing to do

498
00:37:55.750 --> 00:37:57.333
with what happened in the subway.
Alright?

499
00:37:58.708 --> 00:38:00.417
You don't need to pretend with me.

500
00:38:00.542 --> 00:38:01.917
- I'm like you.
- Yeah, sure. Like me.

501
00:38:02.125 --> 00:38:05.208
A thou a month and on contract.
And you a millionaire. Just the same!

502
00:38:05.375 --> 00:38:06.375
We're from the same place.

503
00:38:06.500 --> 00:38:08.542
- From Masnou?
- Much farther.

504
00:38:08.708 --> 00:38:10.500
We can't spend all our lives
on the planet

505
00:38:10.667 --> 00:38:12.208
pretending we're like them.

506
00:38:12.375 --> 00:38:14.750
- Know what I mean?
- No. I don't.

507
00:38:14.917 --> 00:38:18.333
Say it like that and it's like
I was an alien.

508
00:38:18.750 --> 00:38:22.000
- That's just what I mean.
- Yeah, right, hilarious.

509
00:38:22.167 --> 00:38:23.833
When you get back to Planet X,

510
00:38:24.042 --> 00:38:27.375
give ET, Alf and Zoltar
a hug for me.

511
00:38:27.500 --> 00:38:29.583
People can't melt things
with their eyes

512
00:38:29.750 --> 00:38:30.875
or run at that speed!

513
00:38:31.083 --> 00:38:33.458
People can't stop a subway train!

514
00:38:37.458 --> 00:38:40.458
Look, two things.
One, I don't do that stuff.

515
00:38:40.583 --> 00:38:42.583
And two, how do you know?

516
00:38:42.750 --> 00:38:45.708
I can take you to a place
where you can be normal.

517
00:38:45.875 --> 00:38:48.250
We'll go back home with my father.

518
00:38:48.417 --> 00:38:50.833
Yeah, sure, in a UFO. Right.

519
00:38:51.042 --> 00:38:52.917
I'm not the person you're after.

520
00:38:53.125 --> 00:38:55.125
- Besides, I'm late for dinner.
- Wait.

521
00:38:59.250 --> 00:39:01.208
That's why!

522
00:39:01.375 --> 00:39:03.792
You want to stay for her...
Who's that girl?

523
00:39:05.500 --> 00:39:06.500
You read my mind?

524
00:39:06.917 --> 00:39:09.667
I tried to convince you
the easy way.

525
00:39:10.625 --> 00:39:12.583
- The easy way?
- You're staying here

526
00:39:12.750 --> 00:39:15.292
- until my father arrives.
- Get off!

527
00:39:15.792 --> 00:39:17.250
Get off!

528
00:39:22.250 --> 00:39:23.583
Man, look at my clothes!

529
00:39:29.875 --> 00:39:32.292
Sorry, but look what you did
to my clothes.

530
00:39:34.458 --> 00:39:37.667
I knew it.
I knew you were Jan's son!

531
00:39:58.000 --> 00:39:59.250
What's all this about?

532
00:40:00.500 --> 00:40:01.458
Finish him off!

533
00:40:01.583 --> 00:40:03.750
Guys, this is a misunderstanding,
I was going to...

534
00:40:04.542 --> 00:40:05.375
Sorry.

535
00:40:09.500 --> 00:40:10.583
You dropped...

536
00:40:14.042 --> 00:40:15.208
Sorry.

537
00:40:49.000 --> 00:40:50.083
Agata, stop this!

538
00:40:57.625 --> 00:40:59.125
Stop this!

539
00:41:05.792 --> 00:41:07.417
- Get him, get him!
- Get him!

540
00:41:07.542 --> 00:41:09.500
- Where is he?
- Where is he?

541
00:41:10.542 --> 00:41:12.417
- There!
- Who's got him?

542
00:41:13.917 --> 00:41:15.125
He's escaping, that way!

543
00:41:15.542 --> 00:41:18.750
You can escape from here,
but not from who you are.

544
00:41:18.917 --> 00:41:21.125
And you stop bugging me
with that buzzing thing.

545
00:41:21.292 --> 00:41:22.708
It's really unpleasant.

546
00:41:40.750 --> 00:41:43.875
- We won't let him out of the building.
- It won't do any good.

547
00:41:44.083 --> 00:41:46.458
Besides, I know his weak spot now.

548
00:41:46.583 --> 00:41:50.250
Her name's Luisa Lanas.
I want her DNA.

549
00:42:22.500 --> 00:42:24.417
EXPLORING

550
00:42:25.583 --> 00:42:27.708
SAMPLE LOCATED
TYPE: DNA, SUBJECT: LUISA LANAS

551
00:42:32.708 --> 00:42:33.625
DNA ANALYSIS

552
00:43:09.083 --> 00:43:10.083
Shitty gadget!

553
00:43:15.125 --> 00:43:18.667
No, not a shitty gadget.
Small to medium appliance.

554
00:43:19.625 --> 00:43:22.167
Or as I like to say,
good old household goods.

555
00:43:22.500 --> 00:43:24.625
Hey, take it easy, okay!

556
00:43:28.292 --> 00:43:29.417
Bad goods!

557
00:43:30.292 --> 00:43:31.458
No, no, no.

558
00:43:31.792 --> 00:43:34.583
Okay, okay! No, no!

559
00:43:40.917 --> 00:43:41.917
Relax, eh?

560
00:43:44.917 --> 00:43:46.750
Whoah! Whoah!

561
00:43:52.875 --> 00:43:53.875
Back!

562
00:43:54.417 --> 00:43:56.542
Get back, you bug!

563
00:43:56.708 --> 00:43:59.500
Sit! Sit! Whoah!

564
00:44:00.750 --> 00:44:03.167
Hey, you! Come help me,
it's gone mad!

565
00:44:03.333 --> 00:44:04.417
This robot wants to kill me!

566
00:44:04.750 --> 00:44:06.208
Come on!

567
00:44:06.375 --> 00:44:08.208
What are you doing there?
Come and smash it!

568
00:44:09.208 --> 00:44:10.333
Come on!

569
00:44:13.500 --> 00:44:15.167
Hit it, go!

570
00:44:18.833 --> 00:44:19.917
Go on!

571
00:44:26.667 --> 00:44:30.167
Not a word of this to anyone.
Not the hug either.

572
00:44:41.292 --> 00:44:42.458
DNA SENT

573
00:44:49.083 --> 00:44:50.417
Come on, Luisa, answer!

574
00:44:50.542 --> 00:44:53.500
- Answer, please, answer.
- Juan.

575
00:44:56.042 --> 00:44:58.125
- Luisa, where were you?
- Where was I?

576
00:44:58.292 --> 00:45:00.750
Where were you?
Looking like that...

577
00:45:00.917 --> 00:45:02.917
I went to the restaurant,
but you weren't there.

578
00:45:03.125 --> 00:45:05.500
Yeah, and wait another hour for you.

579
00:45:05.667 --> 00:45:07.542
If you didn't want dinner with me,
you could've said.

580
00:45:07.708 --> 00:45:09.167
Not want dinner with you?

581
00:45:09.333 --> 00:45:11.583
Of course I did, very much,

582
00:45:11.750 --> 00:45:13.583
but something crazy
happened to me.

583
00:45:13.750 --> 00:45:17.042
- Crazier than standing me up?
- Yes.

584
00:45:17.208 --> 00:45:20.542
- What?
- I don't quite know yet.

585
00:45:21.500 --> 00:45:22.542
Luisa, what are you doing?

586
00:45:23.625 --> 00:45:26.500
If I drink a bit more,
maybe I'll believe you.

587
00:45:27.500 --> 00:45:28.250
Look.

588
00:45:29.333 --> 00:45:30.583
- Jaime again.
- Don't answer it!

589
00:45:30.750 --> 00:45:32.000
- Why not?
- Just in case.

590
00:45:32.167 --> 00:45:33.500
- In case of what?
- Well...

591
00:45:35.042 --> 00:45:36.875
Shit, bad signal!

592
00:45:38.500 --> 00:45:40.458
This... Luisa, look...

593
00:45:40.583 --> 00:45:43.292
I know what I'm going
to tell you sounds weird,

594
00:45:43.458 --> 00:45:44.542
so I'll say it straight out.

595
00:45:45.500 --> 00:45:48.500
I just caught a smart
vacuum robot with 6 legs

596
00:45:48.667 --> 00:45:50.042
sending your DNA to someone.

597
00:45:50.208 --> 00:45:52.000
Please, when you hear
my message, call me,

598
00:45:52.167 --> 00:45:54.875
I'm coming over with this beast
so you'll believe me.

599
00:45:55.792 --> 00:45:57.792
I know your address
from your resume.

600
00:45:58.000 --> 00:45:59.750
I haven't seen any emails,
or Facebook or anything.

601
00:45:59.917 --> 00:46:02.625
Don't be suspicious of me,
like your friend Laurita86.

602
00:46:04.375 --> 00:46:05.375
Shit.

603
00:46:05.500 --> 00:46:07.333
- Go on, apologize.
- Really, Luisa.

604
00:46:07.500 --> 00:46:08.875
I'd love to tell you,

605
00:46:09.083 --> 00:46:11.292
but I need a few days
to take it all in.

606
00:46:11.458 --> 00:46:13.417
If I say it straight out,
you'll think it's crazy.

607
00:46:13.542 --> 00:46:16.292
But not "crazy" crazy, no.
Crazy as in "sick".

608
00:46:16.458 --> 00:46:18.833
Okay, better tell me now
while I'm wasted.

609
00:46:19.042 --> 00:46:21.417
This wine cost a fortune
and I have to finish it.

610
00:46:21.542 --> 00:46:23.750
Luisa, I can't tell you anything.

611
00:46:23.917 --> 00:46:24.833
Why?

612
00:46:25.042 --> 00:46:27.375
Because I have to go
and talk to my parents.

613
00:46:27.500 --> 00:46:28.292
- Your parents?
- Yes.

614
00:46:28.458 --> 00:46:30.250
- How old are you, 12?
- Yes. No.

615
00:46:30.417 --> 00:46:31.458
Cut the crap, Juan.

616
00:46:31.583 --> 00:46:33.250
We both know what's going on.

617
00:46:33.500 --> 00:46:36.625
You know, I know,
and so did Rober.

618
00:46:36.792 --> 00:46:39.375
Years have gone by,
but we still like each other.

619
00:46:39.500 --> 00:46:41.000
Always have.

620
00:46:41.167 --> 00:46:43.625
So cut the crap
and come up with me.

621
00:46:43.792 --> 00:46:46.750
If girl like you
asks me to come upstairs,

622
00:46:46.917 --> 00:46:48.167
I'm up there like a buffalo.

623
00:46:48.333 --> 00:46:51.500
I would, but no one's
ever asked me before.

624
00:46:51.667 --> 00:46:53.792
But if I let something happen
between us tonight,

625
00:46:54.000 --> 00:46:56.208
it'd make me the worst person
in the world.

626
00:46:57.333 --> 00:46:59.083
What are you doing, leaving?

627
00:46:59.667 --> 00:47:01.500
Hey! Hey!

628
00:47:02.625 --> 00:47:04.500
Fine, then go.

629
00:47:04.667 --> 00:47:08.042
Go get your parents
to make you a cup of cocoa!

630
00:47:08.208 --> 00:47:11.125
What more do I need
to get a snog out of you?!

631
00:47:11.708 --> 00:47:15.667
You're a little kid!
Go back to kindergarten, coward!

632
00:47:50.708 --> 00:47:52.500
I really am smashed.

633
00:48:01.083 --> 00:48:02.542
Where do you think
you're going with that?

634
00:48:04.375 --> 00:48:05.833
Hell of a technical service.

635
00:48:17.625 --> 00:48:20.750
What is it with you all
and that girl?

636
00:48:21.833 --> 00:48:23.083
She's not that great.

637
00:48:24.458 --> 00:48:27.125
If you help me, Luisa can be yours.

638
00:48:59.750 --> 00:49:02.792
I knew it.
When I saw the news, I knew it.

639
00:49:03.000 --> 00:49:04.125
Get inside.

640
00:49:04.708 --> 00:49:07.500
What did you want me to do?
Stand by with my arms crossed?

641
00:49:08.917 --> 00:49:11.417
I told your mother no,
you're not a dickhead.

642
00:49:11.542 --> 00:49:13.042
Okay, I got a bit overexcited.

643
00:49:13.208 --> 00:49:15.542
It's no big deal if I stop
a train every 30 years.

644
00:49:15.708 --> 00:49:17.625
No? You should've acted
like a normal person.

645
00:49:17.792 --> 00:49:19.500
But I'm not normal, Dad.

646
00:49:19.625 --> 00:49:21.542
- You and Mom knew that.
- Son!

647
00:49:21.708 --> 00:49:23.208
- What do you want?
- To know the truth.

648
00:49:23.375 --> 00:49:25.458
No, do you want fried eggs
and bacon for breakfast

649
00:49:25.583 --> 00:49:27.917
or pork scratching.
You look thin, son.

650
00:49:28.125 --> 00:49:30.792
I don't want anything.
Well, one thing.

651
00:49:31.000 --> 00:49:33.875
I want you to answer
a very simple question.

652
00:49:34.083 --> 00:49:35.292
- Go on.
- Go on.

653
00:49:35.458 --> 00:49:38.292
Tell me, please,
that you're my parents.

654
00:49:42.625 --> 00:49:43.625
Don't shut me out!

655
00:49:43.792 --> 00:49:45.458
Speak up, the tension's choking me!

656
00:49:46.125 --> 00:49:48.000
Tension, no, it's the trip,
you're just tired.

657
00:49:48.167 --> 00:49:49.458
Come on, relax.

658
00:49:49.583 --> 00:49:52.000
Of course we're your parents.
What's this about?

659
00:49:52.167 --> 00:49:53.583
Let's talk about
the day I was born.

660
00:49:53.750 --> 00:49:55.625
Mom, how long were you in labor?

661
00:49:57.292 --> 00:49:59.000
- I don't remember now.
- What are you saying?

662
00:49:59.167 --> 00:50:00.208
I'm an only child!

663
00:50:00.375 --> 00:50:02.125
Your mother and I don't have
the mind for such things,

664
00:50:02.292 --> 00:50:04.125
it was a long time ago.
What's wrong with you?

665
00:50:04.625 --> 00:50:06.042
I met someone.

666
00:50:06.208 --> 00:50:07.500
- A girl?
- No.

667
00:50:08.583 --> 00:50:11.083
Someone who told me
some very strange things.

668
00:50:11.250 --> 00:50:13.083
Well, a girl too,
but that's another issue.

669
00:50:13.458 --> 00:50:15.250
She told me she wants
to take me home.

670
00:50:15.917 --> 00:50:19.458
But not this home, no.
Way out to another galaxy!

671
00:50:19.583 --> 00:50:20.833
And don't say it's the weed,

672
00:50:21.042 --> 00:50:23.333
that was a long time ago
and not that much.

673
00:50:23.500 --> 00:50:27.792
So tell me, please,
if I'm from another galaxy or not.

674
00:50:29.667 --> 00:50:31.875
If you hadn't stopped that train...

675
00:50:32.083 --> 00:50:34.833
So, yes.
This is goddamn incredible!

676
00:50:35.042 --> 00:50:37.542
I'll tell you one thing.
I think it's terrible

677
00:50:37.708 --> 00:50:38.792
that you didn't tell me anything.

678
00:50:39.000 --> 00:50:40.625
Son, to me you're just like
any other boy.

679
00:50:40.792 --> 00:50:43.458
Yes, but with one slight detail.
I'm an alien!

680
00:50:43.583 --> 00:50:45.292
Nobody needs to know.

681
00:50:45.458 --> 00:50:47.458
They tried to kidnap me, Dad!

682
00:50:47.583 --> 00:50:48.875
Who says they won't again?

683
00:50:49.083 --> 00:50:50.500
Now you do have to eat more,

684
00:50:50.625 --> 00:50:53.292
you're too thin to face
the forces of the universe.

685
00:50:53.458 --> 00:50:55.417
Maria, please.
Enough of the movie stuff.

686
00:50:56.875 --> 00:50:59.125
It's time you saw it.

687
00:50:59.292 --> 00:51:01.875
Juan, we said no,
whatever happened.

688
00:51:02.083 --> 00:51:03.875
See what? You're scaring me.

689
00:51:08.125 --> 00:51:10.333
- Come here.
- Go in, son.

690
00:51:20.792 --> 00:51:22.333
Ready?

691
00:51:27.875 --> 00:51:30.417
Does it ring a bell?

692
00:51:30.542 --> 00:51:32.792
Tell me that's not
what I think it is.

693
00:51:33.000 --> 00:51:35.875
You came inside this, son,
we don't know from where.

694
00:51:36.083 --> 00:51:38.583
This doesn't exactly
come from Martorell.

695
00:51:38.750 --> 00:51:39.750
What did you want us to do?

696
00:51:39.917 --> 00:51:41.292
I wanted to call the police.
She was the one who...

697
00:51:41.458 --> 00:51:43.750
The police. Great, really.

698
00:51:43.917 --> 00:51:46.500
You're goddamn model parents.
Congratulations.

699
00:51:46.667 --> 00:51:48.250
- Thank you.
- Be quiet.

700
00:51:58.542 --> 00:51:59.458
<i>Hello, son.</i>

701
00:52:00.000 --> 00:52:01.583
- Watch out.
<i>- If you're watching this,</i>

702
00:52:01.750 --> 00:52:02.750
<i>things got complicated</i>

703
00:52:02.917 --> 00:52:04.750
<i>and we had to send you
far away from Chiton.</i>

704
00:52:04.917 --> 00:52:07.708
<i>But thanks to your extraordinary,
amazing abilities,</i>

705
00:52:07.875 --> 00:52:10.500
<i>I guess you activated this mechanism</i>

706
00:52:10.625 --> 00:52:13.500
<i>at the age of 3 or 4.</i>

707
00:52:13.917 --> 00:52:15.625
Hey, I already had an inkling.

708
00:52:15.792 --> 00:52:17.250
<i>But this is hard to explain,</i>

709
00:52:17.417 --> 00:52:20.125
<i>so I'll used these two puppets.</i>

710
00:52:20.292 --> 00:52:22.750
<i>This is Skorba. I'm Skorba!</i>

711
00:52:22.917 --> 00:52:26.667
<i>I'm very bad and have all of Chiton's
inhabitants under submission.</i>

712
00:52:26.833 --> 00:52:29.333
<i>And this is me, your father.</i>

713
00:52:29.500 --> 00:52:32.625
<i>I won't allow it! With my science
I'll create the perfect weapon</i>

714
00:52:32.792 --> 00:52:34.458
<i>to defeat you!</i>

715
00:52:34.583 --> 00:52:37.375
<i>I hope you're starting
to understand who you are.</i>

716
00:52:38.417 --> 00:52:40.042
Yes, I understand perfectly.

717
00:52:40.208 --> 00:52:42.208
<i>You won't defeat me
with any weapon!</i>

718
00:52:42.375 --> 00:52:44.750
<i>It's not any weapon,
it's the ultimate weapon.</i>

719
00:52:44.917 --> 00:52:48.500
<i>When my son is born,
wind will come from his mouth,</i>

720
00:52:48.625 --> 00:52:51.708
<i>fire from his eyes.
He'll be quick as a flash.</i>

721
00:52:51.875 --> 00:52:55.042
<i>And flying through the galaxy
he'll destroy your empire.</i>

722
00:52:55.208 --> 00:52:56.250
Did he say I'll fly?

723
00:52:56.417 --> 00:52:59.458
<i>Skorba will be looking for you.
Where did your son go?</i>

724
00:52:59.583 --> 00:53:01.667
<i>Left or right?</i>

725
00:53:01.833 --> 00:53:03.333
<i>Left, right.</i>

726
00:53:03.500 --> 00:53:04.875
Go on, tell him.

727
00:53:05.083 --> 00:53:07.208
<i>Son,
this is an interactive hologram.</i>

728
00:53:07.375 --> 00:53:09.167
<i>You have to answer:
left or right.</i>

729
00:53:09.333 --> 00:53:12.417
Until say which one,
the "phonogram" can't go on.

730
00:53:12.667 --> 00:53:15.417
- The fight.
- <i>Good, you said right.</i>

731
00:53:15.542 --> 00:53:18.208
<i>That means you're too little
and didn't understand a thing.</i>

732
00:53:18.375 --> 00:53:22.333
<i>It's about misleading Skorba,
not giving yourself away.</i>

733
00:53:22.500 --> 00:53:24.458
<i>But never mind,
you have to grow up</i>

734
00:53:24.583 --> 00:53:26.542
<i>to reach the intellectual level
of an adult.</i>

735
00:53:26.708 --> 00:53:28.917
<i>Don't worry,
one day you'll be ready.</i>

736
00:53:29.125 --> 00:53:31.458
<i>And when that day comes,
just get in the rocket</i>

737
00:53:31.583 --> 00:53:34.833
<i>and it'll take you back
to Chiton to save us, son.</i>

738
00:53:36.333 --> 00:53:38.208
<i>You're our only hope.</i>

739
00:53:43.333 --> 00:53:46.750
Well, this message must be
from ages ago.

740
00:53:46.917 --> 00:53:50.417
They must've found a way
to sort out their stuff.

741
00:53:51.500 --> 00:53:54.167
And not a word
to anyone about this.

742
00:53:54.333 --> 00:53:57.125
Especially to Uncle Toni­n,
three shots and he blabs everything.

743
00:53:57.292 --> 00:53:58.625
I'm not saying a word,

744
00:53:58.792 --> 00:54:00.292
but I think they're waiting
for you on that planet.

745
00:54:00.458 --> 00:54:03.375
Yeah, right, now the invasion
of this tyrant is my fault.

746
00:54:03.500 --> 00:54:06.417
They must've done something too.
I'd have to hear the other side.

747
00:54:06.542 --> 00:54:09.417
It's so easy to judge people
from other galaxies.

748
00:54:09.542 --> 00:54:11.000
Mom, leave that,
don't touch anything!

749
00:54:11.167 --> 00:54:13.208
Finally a Lopez can do
something important.

750
00:54:13.375 --> 00:54:16.417
I once fixed Sito Pons' motorbike,
I know that's nothing, but...

751
00:54:16.542 --> 00:54:18.250
This month's very bad for me.

752
00:54:18.417 --> 00:54:20.083
I'm doing the dispatches,
the mortgage...

753
00:54:20.250 --> 00:54:22.625
Are they going to do
my quarterly sales tax for me?

754
00:54:22.792 --> 00:54:25.250
The oppressed citizens of Chiton,
Chiton, whatever it's called?

755
00:54:26.167 --> 00:54:28.542
- So every man for himself.
- No, son, no!

756
00:54:28.708 --> 00:54:30.542
They said you're their last hope.

757
00:54:30.708 --> 00:54:32.333
Yes, their last hope, my ass!

758
00:54:32.500 --> 00:54:33.417
Watch your mouth!

759
00:54:33.542 --> 00:54:36.375
How can I go to outer space
without insurance or anything?

760
00:54:36.500 --> 00:54:38.708
Besides, Dad, you always
told me not to stand out.

761
00:54:38.875 --> 00:54:40.833
Sure, but now we know who you are,

762
00:54:41.042 --> 00:54:42.708
you can't act like
you're not who you are.

763
00:54:43.833 --> 00:54:46.292
First, talk properly,
you're unintelligible.

764
00:54:46.458 --> 00:54:47.917
And second, I'm outta here.

765
00:54:49.208 --> 00:54:51.667
Juanito, son. Just in case,
I'll make you a suit from this,

766
00:54:51.833 --> 00:54:54.875
- it looks like good fabric.
- I'm not putting on anything.

767
00:54:55.083 --> 00:54:57.750
A superhero can't go around
tearing ordinary clothes.

768
00:54:57.917 --> 00:55:01.417
- Superheroes don't exist!
- What do we know, son?

769
00:55:01.542 --> 00:55:03.250
Look. I'll just make it
and you can try it on.

770
00:55:03.417 --> 00:55:07.292
- I'm so excited...
- I'm not putting on any suit, period!

771
00:55:24.000 --> 00:55:26.167
Aren't you going to say anything?

772
00:55:26.333 --> 00:55:28.292
It looks so bad on you,
I can't even laugh.

773
00:55:28.458 --> 00:55:31.500
It's a nice, standard-issue supersuit.

774
00:55:31.667 --> 00:55:34.208
With a wig, he's a dead ringer
for the Queen of the Mardi Gras.

775
00:55:34.375 --> 00:55:37.542
- I'm taking it off, it's over.
- No, come here, hold on.

776
00:55:37.708 --> 00:55:40.500
Maybe if i put
a bit of a dart here...

777
00:55:40.625 --> 00:55:43.500
- or some shoulder pads...
- No, shoulder pads, no way!

778
00:55:43.667 --> 00:55:44.750
He look like a junkie
in a tracksuit.

779
00:55:44.917 --> 00:55:47.000
He just needs the flute,
the dog and the chocolate pastry.

780
00:55:47.167 --> 00:55:48.500
Look at Dad. Say something.

781
00:55:48.667 --> 00:55:51.000
A couple of washes
will shrink it to fit.

782
00:55:51.167 --> 00:55:52.500
Besides, you're a growing boy.

783
00:55:52.625 --> 00:55:53.625
Yeah, a growing boy...

784
00:55:53.792 --> 00:55:56.583
Look, I copied this
from the supermen movies.

785
00:55:56.750 --> 00:56:00.042
If you get cold, put it here,
it makes a nice shawl.

786
00:56:00.208 --> 00:56:01.875
No, it's meant to be a cape.

787
00:56:02.083 --> 00:56:04.250
- It's for flying.
- So you can really fly?

788
00:56:05.167 --> 00:56:06.167
Apparently.

789
00:56:06.333 --> 00:56:08.208
That man from the spaceship
mentioned fire and flying.

790
00:56:08.375 --> 00:56:12.000
That man from the spaceship
is my father, he has a name.

791
00:56:12.167 --> 00:56:14.833
- What name?
- I don't know right now.

792
00:56:16.333 --> 00:56:19.167
I'm your father too,
my name's Juan Antonio Lopez

793
00:56:19.333 --> 00:56:21.125
and I'm telling you
you have to learn how to fly.

794
00:56:21.292 --> 00:56:24.000
You may need it one day,
you never know.

795
00:56:24.167 --> 00:56:26.875
Yeah, sure, learn how to fly.
How do you do that?

796
00:56:34.792 --> 00:56:37.042
Someone from town
is going to see me like this!

797
00:56:37.208 --> 00:56:40.250
C'mon, today's the day.
Try to fly!

798
00:56:40.417 --> 00:56:42.833
Sure, try to fly.
Like it was so easy!

799
00:56:43.042 --> 00:56:46.583
Flap like a magpie,
and watch out for the trees!

800
00:56:46.750 --> 00:56:49.292
- That's it, go on.
- Let him concentrate.

801
00:56:50.708 --> 00:56:52.208
Flap wider!

802
00:56:52.708 --> 00:56:56.250
- Like this.
- Not so bunched up. More!

803
00:56:56.833 --> 00:56:58.500
- There.
- Nothing.

804
00:56:58.625 --> 00:57:02.042
- What's he doing with his fist?
- That's it, there!

805
00:57:02.208 --> 00:57:03.292
- Try that!
- Go on!

806
00:57:05.583 --> 00:57:07.250
Nothing, it doesn't work.

807
00:57:07.417 --> 00:57:09.292
I think you'd better jump.

808
00:57:09.458 --> 00:57:11.833
Yeah, sure, jump.
I'll bust my goddamn head!

809
00:57:12.042 --> 00:57:13.667
Maybe this flying thing
is activated in the air.

810
00:57:13.833 --> 00:57:16.417
Trust in yourself
as we trust in you, son!

811
00:57:16.542 --> 00:57:18.542
- That's it.
- I know you'll fly!

812
00:57:18.708 --> 00:57:21.125
Move, that way.

813
00:57:38.375 --> 00:57:42.333
- God, he sure hit the dirt.
- Son, everything alright?

814
00:57:43.500 --> 00:57:45.542
Look how well you get up.

815
00:57:45.708 --> 00:57:47.917
- That's great.
- Does anything hurt?

816
00:57:49.917 --> 00:57:52.208
- It's my fault for listening to you.
- But son...

817
00:57:52.375 --> 00:57:53.792
- You'll get it next time.
- Yes, next time.

818
00:57:54.000 --> 00:57:55.292
Next time you jump off!

819
00:57:55.458 --> 00:57:58.250
No, I said there was
no basis to this.

820
00:57:58.417 --> 00:57:59.458
You're just a little imprecise.

821
00:57:59.583 --> 00:58:02.083
You need to get it right, that's all.

822
00:58:11.292 --> 00:58:13.375
Freak, you're a freak.

823
00:58:15.083 --> 00:58:18.292
Watch it, you're talking to
the hope of another galaxy.

824
00:58:18.458 --> 00:58:21.125
- The galaxy of the tacky, huh?
- You're wearing panties!

825
00:58:22.250 --> 00:58:24.250
They're not panties, you brat!

826
00:58:24.417 --> 00:58:25.542
Maybe I'll beat you up

827
00:58:25.708 --> 00:58:28.042
and you'll see who
the ultimate weapon is.

828
00:58:28.208 --> 00:58:31.875
- You gonna hit us with your handbag?
- Is the "S" for sissy?

829
00:58:32.375 --> 00:58:35.417
- Or subnormal.
- Or sausage-sucker.

830
00:58:41.917 --> 00:58:44.625
What? You're not laughing
so hard now, eh?

831
00:58:46.708 --> 00:58:48.208
- Run.
- Run,run!

832
00:58:53.917 --> 00:58:55.625
Holy guacamole!

833
00:58:56.542 --> 00:58:58.708
Juan, look! Look, Juan!

834
00:58:58.875 --> 00:59:01.417
- He's not flying, but he is levitating!
- Holy shit!

835
00:59:01.542 --> 00:59:03.250
- Saint Teresa!
- The Calcutta one?

836
00:59:03.417 --> 00:59:05.000
No, Avila. This is a miracle!

837
00:59:15.000 --> 00:59:17.750
- No way your saint does that.
- Where did he go?

838
00:59:51.500 --> 00:59:54.125
- Do you know where I am?
- Sa Cala de Marbres.

839
00:59:54.417 --> 00:59:56.458
- Where?
- In Mallorca.

840
00:59:57.625 --> 00:59:59.042
Mallorca?

841
00:59:59.750 --> 01:00:02.042
Bucks' party got out of hand, eh?

842
01:00:15.042 --> 01:00:16.333
Damn!

843
01:00:34.750 --> 01:00:36.583
Look, you take Txatxarramendi road,

844
01:00:36.750 --> 01:00:37.833
past Legorreta and Kastelleta

845
01:00:38.042 --> 01:00:40.417
and at Amorebieta
you take the A-8 and straight on.

846
01:00:40.542 --> 01:00:43.292
Careful, if the first town
you see is Yiurreta,

847
01:00:43.458 --> 01:00:46.125
you're screwed, kid,
you're in a jam.

848
01:00:46.292 --> 01:00:48.250
You turn the fuck around
back to Ibaneta,

849
01:00:48.417 --> 01:00:51.208
take the shortcut
from Goitzueta to Txoritokieta

850
01:00:51.375 --> 01:00:54.083
and then get the fucking A-8
just past Guantxoritzketa.

851
01:00:54.250 --> 01:00:55.833
A hell of a way around.

852
01:00:56.500 --> 01:00:58.583
Got it, or do I explain again?

853
01:00:59.292 --> 01:01:01.417
Yes, yes, absolutely clear.

854
01:01:07.375 --> 01:01:09.083
Holy crap!

855
01:01:55.625 --> 01:01:57.625
Mom, it's so obvious,
this is ridiculous.

856
01:01:57.792 --> 01:02:00.333
- You don't notice the bump.
- No, not at all...

857
01:02:00.500 --> 01:02:02.875
And you can wear it all year,
it won't give you a hump.

858
01:02:03.083 --> 01:02:04.500
You'll see the sweat
when spring comes.

859
01:02:04.667 --> 01:02:06.458
- No!
- Don't be tedious, son.

860
01:02:06.583 --> 01:02:08.167
If you get into a galactic tussle,

861
01:02:08.333 --> 01:02:10.583
just rip you clothes off like this,

862
01:02:10.750 --> 01:02:11.667
that's always imposing.

863
01:02:11.833 --> 01:02:13.792
Like I'd tear my clothes,
with what they cost.

864
01:02:14.000 --> 01:02:15.292
- No, I'm not wearing it.
- Listen, Juanito...

865
01:02:26.500 --> 01:02:28.750
- Does Juan live here?
- No.

866
01:02:28.917 --> 01:02:31.208
Are you sure?
Jaime told me he lives here.

867
01:02:31.792 --> 01:02:32.708
Luisa?

868
01:02:33.833 --> 01:02:34.750
What are you doing here?

869
01:02:35.917 --> 01:02:38.000
I found out everything.
How could I not come?

870
01:02:40.375 --> 01:02:43.625
- Relax, she's from this galaxy.
- Ah.

871
01:02:43.792 --> 01:02:44.917
Something to eat?

872
01:02:45.125 --> 01:02:47.500
- You're skin and bone.
- Mom, please.

873
01:02:47.625 --> 01:02:49.542
Forgive us, we're kind of nervous.

874
01:02:49.708 --> 01:02:52.000
It's the first time
Juan's brought a girl home.

875
01:02:52.708 --> 01:02:54.917
That's just the info we needed.

876
01:02:55.125 --> 01:02:57.250
I didn't mean you're an item, eh?

877
01:02:57.417 --> 01:02:59.208
- I didn't mean...
- Dad, please!

878
01:02:59.375 --> 01:03:02.083
We know what "being friends"
means these days.

879
01:03:03.083 --> 01:03:04.167
Like something cool?

880
01:03:04.333 --> 01:03:07.583
- Get them some lemonade, Maria.
- You get it.

881
01:03:07.750 --> 01:03:10.083
- Why didn't you tell me last night?
- I don't know.

882
01:03:10.250 --> 01:03:13.917
- I was afraid I'd look weird...
- But this is beautiful, Juan.

883
01:03:14.125 --> 01:03:18.083
- This is incredible.
- How did you find out...?

884
01:03:18.250 --> 01:03:21.500
Are you alright, Luisa? Your eye...

885
01:03:21.625 --> 01:03:22.583
- My eye?
- Your eye.

886
01:03:23.458 --> 01:03:27.250
It's the excitement.
I know everything and it's beautiful.

887
01:03:27.417 --> 01:03:30.083
They said they want to help you
get back to your true home.

888
01:03:30.250 --> 01:03:33.250
- You met the vacuum lady?
- Yes.

889
01:03:33.417 --> 01:03:35.583
She's really worried about you.

890
01:03:35.750 --> 01:03:38.333
Stop, maybe she didn't tell you
she tried to kidnap me.

891
01:03:38.500 --> 01:03:41.542
Yes. She's as nervous as you
about all this.

892
01:03:41.708 --> 01:03:44.125
About having found you and...

893
01:03:44.292 --> 01:03:47.667
she asked me to apologize to you
for being so brusque.

894
01:03:50.167 --> 01:03:51.750
What, don't you believe me?

895
01:03:51.917 --> 01:03:55.083
- I'm Luisa, why would I deceive you?
- Luisa, you're acting strange.

896
01:03:55.250 --> 01:03:56.667
- What about last night?
- Last night? What?

897
01:03:56.833 --> 01:03:58.083
- Yes, last night.
- Last night?

898
01:03:58.250 --> 01:03:58.875
- Last night.
- Yes?

899
01:03:59.083 --> 01:04:01.500
I think it's as important
or more that all this.

900
01:04:01.625 --> 01:04:05.083
Sure. Last night...
lots of things happened.

901
01:04:06.333 --> 01:04:08.208
I don't know what you mean exactly.

902
01:04:08.375 --> 01:04:11.083
Ask him if it's more or less important
than betraying a friend.

903
01:04:11.250 --> 01:04:13.333
Ask him. Ask him!

904
01:04:13.500 --> 01:04:16.000
What's he saying?
What happened last night?

905
01:04:16.833 --> 01:04:19.667
- What happened?
- I know.

906
01:04:26.042 --> 01:04:28.500
No need to make a big issue
out of it, Juan.

907
01:04:28.667 --> 01:04:31.375
It was a couple of crappy kisses
in a doorway.

908
01:04:31.500 --> 01:04:33.125
Crappy? What's this about?

909
01:04:33.292 --> 01:04:36.167
Maybe you think snogging
in a doorway means we're an item.

910
01:04:36.333 --> 01:04:39.042
Now you're off to Raticuli­n
or whatever galaxy you're from.

911
01:04:39.208 --> 01:04:41.125
What do we do?
One weekend in your constellation

912
01:04:41.292 --> 01:04:42.458
and one in mine?

913
01:04:42.583 --> 01:04:44.500
No! You're a bad kisser,
let me say it again.

914
01:04:44.625 --> 01:04:46.500
But I'm telling you
I don't want to go!

915
01:04:46.625 --> 01:04:48.542
Now I'm taking off
my possible girlfriend hat

916
01:04:48.708 --> 01:04:52.167
and putting on my
citizen-of-this-planet hat.

917
01:04:52.333 --> 01:04:55.292
Do you really think you can
keep living here, doing weird stuff?

918
01:04:55.458 --> 01:04:57.500
It's not weird,
they're superpowers.

919
01:04:58.333 --> 01:04:59.750
Back it up a bit.

920
01:04:59.917 --> 01:05:02.417
Don't call them superpowers,
just super-sight and super-hearing.

921
01:05:02.542 --> 01:05:03.792
And X-rays in my eyes.

922
01:05:04.000 --> 01:05:06.292
Okay, you've got super-sight,
super-hearing and X-rays.

923
01:05:06.458 --> 01:05:09.167
- And I fly.
- You fly as well?

924
01:05:09.333 --> 01:05:11.417
- And super-strength.
- Well, you know what?

925
01:05:11.542 --> 01:05:13.125
Jaime has a superpower too.

926
01:05:13.292 --> 01:05:14.708
He's super-smart.

927
01:05:14.875 --> 01:05:18.083
And he figured us out because
it reeks from miles off.

928
01:05:18.250 --> 01:05:21.250
Or at least sensed it.
He's HR head for some reason.

929
01:05:21.417 --> 01:05:23.208
- Because he knows people.
- I know.

930
01:05:23.375 --> 01:05:26.458
Plus, he was your friend.
And you know he liked me a lot.

931
01:05:26.583 --> 01:05:28.708
And he has his clique,
you might say.

932
01:05:28.875 --> 01:05:31.875
- Do you think I don't care?
- I didn't look like it in the doorway.

933
01:05:32.083 --> 01:05:34.000
Now you know what's
going on with me,

934
01:05:34.167 --> 01:05:37.417
you'll understand that it's always
been hard for me to make friends.

935
01:05:38.250 --> 01:05:41.458
And Jaime always tells me
he's my boss and my friend.

936
01:05:41.583 --> 01:05:44.542
And well, technically
he's not my boss, but...

937
01:05:45.708 --> 01:05:47.250
...he's always been my friend.

938
01:05:48.708 --> 01:05:50.458
And you're right, Luisa.

939
01:05:51.458 --> 01:05:53.208
I have to talk to him first.

940
01:05:53.583 --> 01:05:55.500
I love Jaime a lot.

941
01:05:57.000 --> 01:05:58.417
And he's my only friend.

942
01:06:09.083 --> 01:06:11.500
Don't you dare believe this shit.

943
01:06:15.042 --> 01:06:18.250
Very well.
We'll get him my way.

944
01:06:25.917 --> 01:06:29.000
It seems you didn't understand
anything I said...

945
01:06:33.417 --> 01:06:35.167
Oh, you're into that, eh?

946
01:06:35.333 --> 01:06:37.500
I'm not much,
but I haven't really done it.

947
01:06:37.625 --> 01:06:40.625
But because I haven't tried it,
maybe if we do and it's cool...

948
01:06:42.542 --> 01:06:44.625
Juanito!

949
01:06:44.792 --> 01:06:46.208
Juanito!

950
01:06:46.375 --> 01:06:48.167
- Son, what happened?
- What's wrong?

951
01:06:48.917 --> 01:06:50.542
Oh, my boy. Are you alright?

952
01:06:50.708 --> 01:06:53.500
You argued?
You're starting early!

953
01:07:02.292 --> 01:07:03.458
What's up with her?

954
01:07:07.250 --> 01:07:09.500
- That girl's no good for you.
- Out of the way.

955
01:07:11.167 --> 01:07:12.833
That's not a girl.

956
01:07:14.833 --> 01:07:15.750
See, Dad, it's not that easy!

957
01:07:15.917 --> 01:07:17.833
- Here, my nails are better.
- Get off!

958
01:07:18.042 --> 01:07:19.500
- Look at her!
- She's coming, go!

959
01:07:19.625 --> 01:07:20.667
Here comes the oddball.

960
01:07:20.833 --> 01:07:23.125
- Get your pants off.
- Pull that way.

961
01:07:23.292 --> 01:07:25.042
Stop, or I'll never learn
to do it by myself!

962
01:07:25.208 --> 01:07:27.292
Come on, son,
show her who you are!

963
01:07:27.458 --> 01:07:28.750
- And who am I?
- I don't know!

964
01:07:28.917 --> 01:07:31.458
- Get your pants off!
- Pull!

965
01:07:31.750 --> 01:07:33.500
- She's coming!
- She's coming.

966
01:07:37.708 --> 01:07:40.625
Move, stay over there.
I'll take care of her.

967
01:08:29.000 --> 01:08:31.333
- Wait, wait.
- Maria, be careful.

968
01:08:31.500 --> 01:08:35.167
What did you do to my son?
Tart, oddball, bitch!

969
01:08:35.333 --> 01:08:37.083
Hurting my son?
Don't you touch him!

970
01:08:37.250 --> 01:08:38.458
Woman to woman, come on!

971
01:08:38.583 --> 01:08:40.542
Woman to woman!

972
01:08:42.917 --> 01:08:44.042
Let go of my wife!

973
01:08:44.208 --> 01:08:45.917
Don't bring my mother into this!

974
01:08:58.042 --> 01:09:02.000
Jaime, we're going to need
the real Luisa.

975
01:09:02.167 --> 01:09:05.500
No, no. I did my part.
You don't need me now.

976
01:09:05.625 --> 01:09:07.375
Besides, I'm going now,

977
01:09:07.500 --> 01:09:09.792
I remembered I left
my whites on to wash.

978
01:09:10.000 --> 01:09:12.708
Yes. By the way,
your washing machine's great.

979
01:09:12.875 --> 01:09:15.000
Totally reliable. Hats off.

980
01:09:15.542 --> 01:09:19.583
Jaime, you saw that
I can't bring him here by force.

981
01:09:19.750 --> 01:09:22.833
He has to come himself.
And for this I need bait.

982
01:09:23.542 --> 01:09:26.458
- Help me find the real one.
- That wasn't the deal.

983
01:09:26.583 --> 01:09:28.125
You're wrong.

984
01:09:28.292 --> 01:09:30.417
- You don't need me here.
- You're protecting him now?

985
01:09:31.208 --> 01:09:34.458
- You really believed that drivel?
- Of course I didn't!

986
01:09:34.833 --> 01:09:37.000
But it was kind of the truth.

987
01:09:38.583 --> 01:09:40.625
One moment...

988
01:09:42.042 --> 01:09:44.583
Juan, I forgive you.
And love you.

989
01:09:44.750 --> 01:09:46.792
How could I not forgive you?
You're my only friend too.

990
01:09:47.000 --> 01:09:48.708
But the main thing now
is that Luisa's in danger.

991
01:09:48.875 --> 01:09:50.250
Agata Muller wants to kidnap her!

992
01:09:50.417 --> 01:09:51.708
Yeah, it's wild.
The lady on TV!

993
01:09:52.500 --> 01:09:56.167
Sorry... I think they're
reading my mind.

994
01:10:12.125 --> 01:10:14.083
- You really think you can go now?
- Yes.

995
01:10:14.250 --> 01:10:16.333
- That wasn't a question.
- Ah, no.

996
01:10:17.583 --> 01:10:19.125
Oh, Jaime, Jaime, Jaime...

997
01:10:19.792 --> 01:10:23.083
I'm so sorry. This hurts me
more than it does you.

998
01:10:23.708 --> 01:10:26.833
No, actually I think
it'll hurt you a little more,

999
01:10:27.042 --> 01:10:28.083
unless you help.

1000
01:10:29.250 --> 01:10:33.292
Agata! This isn't the way
to do things! Not like this!

1001
01:10:33.875 --> 01:10:35.708
Do we have the trap ready?

1002
01:10:36.833 --> 01:10:38.792
- It's almost ready.
- Almost ready is no good to me.

1003
01:10:39.000 --> 01:10:40.708
My father's almost here.

1004
01:10:41.333 --> 01:10:44.333
- So where's your real girlfriend?
- She's not my girlfriend! Cut it out!

1005
01:10:44.500 --> 01:10:46.000
Call her what you like!

1006
01:10:46.167 --> 01:10:49.458
- But she's in danger because of you.
- Thanks for the analysis, Mom.

1007
01:10:49.583 --> 01:10:52.333
If you don't want to save
your planet, it's up to you.

1008
01:10:52.500 --> 01:10:54.250
But at least save her.

1009
01:11:06.500 --> 01:11:09.583
- Hello?
- <i>Luisa? Where are you?</i>

1010
01:11:09.750 --> 01:11:11.625
Juan? I can barely hear you.

1011
01:11:11.792 --> 01:11:13.583
Yes, well, it's the signal.

1012
01:11:13.750 --> 01:11:16.125
- Where are you? I'll come get you.
- On my way home.

1013
01:11:16.292 --> 01:11:18.542
- I can meet you there.
- No, no! Not your place!

1014
01:11:18.708 --> 01:11:21.042
Stay where you are,
there are people.

1015
01:11:21.500 --> 01:11:23.708
- I'm at the Arco de Triunfo.
- Really?

1016
01:11:23.875 --> 01:11:27.250
You won't believe it.
Me too! I'll be right there.

1017
01:11:44.625 --> 01:11:45.792
Luisa?

1018
01:11:46.000 --> 01:11:48.250
- What's up with you?
- Me? What's up with you?

1019
01:11:48.417 --> 01:11:49.917
When did we meet?

1020
01:11:50.125 --> 01:11:51.667
What's your favorite drink?

1021
01:11:51.833 --> 01:11:53.625
Do you like black olives
on your pizzas?

1022
01:11:53.792 --> 01:11:56.583
- Juan, you're being an idiot.
- Okay, you're Luisa. No doubt.

1023
01:11:56.750 --> 01:11:58.417
Tell me what's going on.

1024
01:11:58.542 --> 01:12:00.375
Luisa, I'm not normal.

1025
01:12:00.500 --> 01:12:03.083
- I got that. You have some things...
- Some things, sure...

1026
01:12:03.250 --> 01:12:06.375
Like I can melt ice with a look.

1027
01:12:06.500 --> 01:12:09.167
Or I can see through walls.

1028
01:12:09.333 --> 01:12:11.208
Or maybe I sneeze
and knock down a partition.

1029
01:12:11.375 --> 01:12:13.625
Apart from all that,
yes, I'm run-of-the-mill.

1030
01:12:13.792 --> 01:12:16.542
Fine. Is this when I laugh?

1031
01:12:16.708 --> 01:12:18.708
I stopped the subway train.

1032
01:12:18.875 --> 01:12:21.042
I can fly too,
but I found that out today.

1033
01:12:21.583 --> 01:12:24.333
I've been given some dumb excuses
for dumping me,

1034
01:12:24.500 --> 01:12:26.500
- but this is the worst.
- It's not an excuse!

1035
01:12:26.625 --> 01:12:28.875
I'll tell you something.
We weren't even going out.

1036
01:12:29.083 --> 01:12:31.250
- So there's no need to lie.
- It's not a lie!

1037
01:12:31.417 --> 01:12:33.167
- I'm telling you the truth, Luisa.
- Please, Juan.

1038
01:12:33.333 --> 01:12:35.708
All you left out is that
you're an alien.

1039
01:12:36.458 --> 01:12:37.708
What?

1040
01:12:37.875 --> 01:12:39.292
Just what I needed.

1041
01:12:39.458 --> 01:12:41.167
- Don't go too far away.
- How about this:

1042
01:12:41.333 --> 01:12:42.667
If it's all true, show me!

1043
01:12:42.833 --> 01:12:44.417
- Don't talk crap.
- Don't you say you can fly?

1044
01:12:44.542 --> 01:12:46.500
- Then go on, fly. Do something.
- Yeah, fly...

1045
01:12:46.625 --> 01:12:49.542
How can I fly here?
They'll find us!

1046
01:12:49.708 --> 01:12:51.375
- Who?
- Agata Muller!

1047
01:12:51.625 --> 01:12:54.417
She's an alien too,
from the same planet.

1048
01:12:54.542 --> 01:12:55.458
- Your planet?
- Chiton.

1049
01:12:55.583 --> 01:12:56.792
What?

1050
01:12:57.000 --> 01:12:57.917
If you make up a planet,

1051
01:12:58.125 --> 01:13:00.417
don't make it sound like
a village outside of Albacete!

1052
01:13:02.708 --> 01:13:04.375
What?

1053
01:13:05.458 --> 01:13:07.458
- You made a suit and everything?
- My mother made it.

1054
01:13:07.583 --> 01:13:09.458
You mother made you
a suit to dump me?

1055
01:13:11.333 --> 01:13:12.792
Really, Luisa. It's...

1056
01:13:13.833 --> 01:13:16.000
You're making me do this...

1057
01:13:17.167 --> 01:13:18.333
in front of everyone!

1058
01:13:18.500 --> 01:13:21.417
But it's always the same with you.
Always the same!

1059
01:13:22.000 --> 01:13:23.417
You're no help at all.

1060
01:13:27.167 --> 01:13:29.875
See that? The Arco de Triunfo?

1061
01:13:30.083 --> 01:13:32.667
I'll loop through it
and be right back.

1062
01:13:35.708 --> 01:13:38.667
I've never been dumped
in such an original way before.

1063
01:13:46.500 --> 01:13:49.417
Hey, smartass, where do
you think you're going?

1064
01:13:49.542 --> 01:13:52.917
If you want to work
this area, pretty boy,

1065
01:13:53.125 --> 01:13:56.083
you have to get permission
from Jeferson Noruega, like everyone!

1066
01:13:56.250 --> 01:13:58.333
Sorry, I think there's been a mistake.

1067
01:13:58.500 --> 01:14:00.292
- I'm the real thing.
- That's a lie.

1068
01:14:01.208 --> 01:14:03.250
I know the real one: Osvaldo.

1069
01:14:03.417 --> 01:14:05.667
And he does Robocop
Saturdays on Las Ramblas.

1070
01:14:07.500 --> 01:14:09.500
We're all very confused.

1071
01:14:09.625 --> 01:14:11.458
- This isn't a costume.
- Yeah, right.

1072
01:14:11.583 --> 01:14:13.250
You're in your pajamas, man!

1073
01:14:13.417 --> 01:14:16.083
Jef, we keep up the quality
so this dude can screw it up.

1074
01:14:16.250 --> 01:14:17.333
You...

1075
01:14:17.500 --> 01:14:19.458
Two things.
One, these are not pajamas.

1076
01:14:19.583 --> 01:14:22.292
And two, I really save people.

1077
01:14:22.625 --> 01:14:24.625
Luisa...

1078
01:14:27.167 --> 01:14:27.792
Luisa?

1079
01:14:31.833 --> 01:14:33.875
- Get in!
- Drive!

1080
01:14:35.708 --> 01:14:36.875
Luisa!

1081
01:14:37.208 --> 01:14:39.625
- Luisa!
- Wait a moment.

1082
01:14:39.792 --> 01:14:41.750
You're not leaving
until you tell us where you got it.

1083
01:14:41.917 --> 01:14:44.625
- I don't want any trouble, okay?
- Oh, no?

1084
01:14:52.208 --> 01:14:54.250
<i>It's me again, son of Jan.</i>

1085
01:14:54.417 --> 01:14:57.917
<i>I don't want to hurt Luisa,
so don't make me waste my time.</i>

1086
01:14:58.125 --> 01:15:00.375
- Don't you dare!
- No?

1087
01:15:01.250 --> 01:15:03.500
Get outta here, you clown!

1088
01:15:03.667 --> 01:15:06.292
- What do you want from me?
- Get outta here!

1089
01:15:14.292 --> 01:15:15.500
The sword!

1090
01:15:17.208 --> 01:15:19.500
<i>Accept it, you're not the others.</i>

1091
01:15:21.500 --> 01:15:23.125
- Fuck, you idiot!
- Sorry, man!

1092
01:15:23.292 --> 01:15:25.542
- You tore my suit!
- It was already torn.

1093
01:15:25.708 --> 01:15:26.833
Like hell it was!

1094
01:15:28.000 --> 01:15:30.292
<i>My father will be here soon.
Join us</i>

1095
01:15:30.458 --> 01:15:33.167
<i>and together we'll rule
these pathetic creatures.</i>

1096
01:15:40.458 --> 01:15:42.500
- <i>I'll wait for you here.</i>
- Where are you?

1097
01:15:42.625 --> 01:15:45.500
- Where's Luisa?
- <i>You know where to find me.</i>

1098
01:16:17.792 --> 01:16:19.708
Excuse me, Agata Muller's office?

1099
01:16:48.333 --> 01:16:49.500
- Juan, help us!
- Where were you?

1100
01:16:49.667 --> 01:16:51.833
- Help us, look at us!
- Get us out of here!

1101
01:16:52.042 --> 01:16:53.458
- Use your power!
- And tell me what's happening!

1102
01:16:53.583 --> 01:16:56.042
- Careful, it's a trap.
- Where were you?

1103
01:16:56.208 --> 01:16:59.125
<i>It you speak at the same time,
I can't understand you.</i>

1104
01:16:59.292 --> 01:17:01.042
Don't get out of the elevator,
it's a trap.

1105
01:17:05.875 --> 01:17:08.250
- Juan, what's going on?
- I told you, Luisa.

1106
01:17:08.417 --> 01:17:09.583
He has powers, I've seen it!

1107
01:17:09.750 --> 01:17:13.083
- People don't have 'powers'.
- Juanito, she doesn't believe it.

1108
01:17:13.250 --> 01:17:14.750
- Go on, fly.
- How can I fly?

1109
01:17:14.917 --> 01:17:17.083
We're inside.
I'll bang myself silly!

1110
01:17:17.250 --> 01:17:20.292
- Then super-strength or super-vision.
- It's super-sight!

1111
01:17:20.458 --> 01:17:22.542
Supervision is something else,
that's supervising!

1112
01:17:22.708 --> 01:17:25.208
You don't have to correct me
in front of her, eh, Juanito?

1113
01:17:25.375 --> 01:17:26.875
You guys are terrible!

1114
01:17:28.542 --> 01:17:29.625
Your underwear.

1115
01:17:31.750 --> 01:17:33.583
You're wearing a black bra...

1116
01:17:33.750 --> 01:17:35.375
with a bit of padding.

1117
01:17:36.083 --> 01:17:39.542
You actually wear panties...
and they're from another set.

1118
01:17:42.625 --> 01:17:46.083
- You have a tattoo?
- Wow, that's hot.

1119
01:17:46.250 --> 01:17:47.667
It says 'Rober'?

1120
01:17:48.500 --> 01:17:50.458
Didn't you tell me
you were half going out?

1121
01:17:50.583 --> 01:17:54.333
- Don't talk about Rober now!
- I see something too.

1122
01:17:54.500 --> 01:17:57.833
Yes, you have a mole.
Just there, above the...

1123
01:17:58.042 --> 01:18:00.708
You don't see a thing!
And untie me!

1124
01:18:01.833 --> 01:18:02.667
Juan!

1125
01:18:03.375 --> 01:18:04.708
What's wrong with you?

1126
01:18:05.375 --> 01:18:06.125
Juan!

1127
01:18:06.667 --> 01:18:08.083
<i>- I hear a noise.
- What noise?</i>

1128
01:18:08.250 --> 01:18:10.167
- <i>A noise.</i>
- Suffer, suffer...

1129
01:18:13.708 --> 01:18:14.792
The noise!

1130
01:18:18.542 --> 01:18:19.875
It must be the speakers.

1131
01:18:20.083 --> 01:18:21.667
Luisa, we have to buck him up
so he gets strong.

1132
01:18:22.500 --> 01:18:23.917
Juan, I forgive you.

1133
01:18:24.125 --> 01:18:25.625
I know you were after Luisa,
but I'm getting over it.

1134
01:18:25.792 --> 01:18:27.583
Why bring that up now?

1135
01:18:27.750 --> 01:18:29.250
- So you wangled me the job.
- Luisa,

1136
01:18:29.417 --> 01:18:31.500
are we doing what
we're doing or not here?

1137
01:18:32.583 --> 01:18:35.875
Tell him you like him too.
You'd tattoo his name on your thigh.

1138
01:18:37.250 --> 01:18:39.042
I'm serious! Say something nice!

1139
01:18:39.667 --> 01:18:41.583
Juan, this...

1140
01:18:43.583 --> 01:18:44.708
You're, you're...

1141
01:18:48.000 --> 01:18:48.917
really sweet.

1142
01:18:50.875 --> 01:18:53.042
What's that shit?
You almost finished him off!

1143
01:18:53.208 --> 01:18:55.458
- Tell him something epic!
- Yes,yes...

1144
01:18:55.583 --> 01:18:57.417
Juan, when...

1145
01:18:57.542 --> 01:19:00.667
when I said a Spanish superhero
was pathetic,

1146
01:19:00.833 --> 01:19:02.208
it's because I didn't know
that you were one.

1147
01:19:02.375 --> 01:19:04.333
Actually, I still think it's pathetic.

1148
01:19:04.500 --> 01:19:07.417
As for the suit, don't worry,
we can do something, alright?

1149
01:19:07.542 --> 01:19:10.333
So gather strength from somewhere
and get us out of here now!

1150
01:19:12.542 --> 01:19:15.250
It's not working.
It never fails in the movies.

1151
01:19:15.708 --> 01:19:17.042
What a shitty superhero!

1152
01:19:19.042 --> 01:19:20.083
- What did you say?
- Sorry,

1153
01:19:20.250 --> 01:19:22.292
but look what he's like
with just some buzzing.

1154
01:19:24.625 --> 01:19:27.333
- No, repeat what you said.
- What a shitty superhero!

1155
01:19:27.500 --> 01:19:29.542
Look at him lying there. Pathetic!

1156
01:19:29.708 --> 01:19:32.125
- You failure.
- Insult him more.

1157
01:19:32.750 --> 01:19:35.083
Shitty superhero!

1158
01:19:37.667 --> 01:19:38.792
It's working.

1159
01:19:39.000 --> 01:19:40.375
Insulting him works.

1160
01:19:52.667 --> 01:19:54.333
It's time to go home.

1161
01:20:00.375 --> 01:20:01.583
- Loser!
- Useless!

1162
01:20:01.750 --> 01:20:04.667
Superhero, sure
Supershithead, that's you!

1163
01:20:04.833 --> 01:20:06.375
- Idiot!
- Incompetent!

1164
01:20:06.500 --> 01:20:09.750
- Unpunctual!
- You're a flop, a mediocre superhero!

1165
01:20:09.917 --> 01:20:12.333
You're embarrassing to me.
Second rate!

1166
01:20:12.500 --> 01:20:14.625
Your English is crap,
intermediate level.

1167
01:20:14.792 --> 01:20:18.125
And your Powerpoint is awful!

1168
01:20:18.292 --> 01:20:20.667
- You kiss real shitty!
- Really?

1169
01:20:20.833 --> 01:20:21.750
I knew it.

1170
01:20:21.917 --> 01:20:24.167
How could he kiss right
with that cop mustache?

1171
01:20:40.917 --> 01:20:41.708
Dad!

1172
01:20:42.250 --> 01:20:45.500
- First of all, good morning.
- I was looking forward to seeing you.

1173
01:20:45.667 --> 01:20:47.875
And I'm looking forward
to seeing Jan's son!

1174
01:20:49.583 --> 01:20:52.333
- He's in my power.
- Let's see if that's true.

1175
01:20:57.333 --> 01:20:59.167
You're making a fool of yourself.

1176
01:20:59.333 --> 01:21:02.708
Not any fool, no.
The biggest fool in the galaxy!

1177
01:21:02.875 --> 01:21:04.542
These people know lots of planets.

1178
01:21:04.708 --> 01:21:07.083
They'll laugh at you
in all of the constellations.

1179
01:21:07.250 --> 01:21:09.875
You know where Andromeda is?
Well, way beyond that

1180
01:21:10.083 --> 01:21:12.333
they'll laugh at how pathetic you are!

1181
01:21:50.083 --> 01:21:51.583
If you can fly,
I don't get why

1182
01:21:51.750 --> 01:21:54.167
you're late for work every day.

1183
01:21:54.708 --> 01:21:56.792
Now you know I'm a superhero,

1184
01:21:57.000 --> 01:21:59.292
don't tell anyone at the office.
Some people really gossip.

1185
01:21:59.458 --> 01:22:01.417
Well, you being a superhero,
we'll see about that.

1186
01:22:01.542 --> 01:22:03.750
- Shall I let go of you?
- No, no!

1187
01:22:03.917 --> 01:22:04.833
- I believe you.
- Alright.

1188
01:22:05.042 --> 01:22:06.375
Where do we go now?

1189
01:22:06.500 --> 01:22:08.917
Where all 30-year-olds go
when they're in a spot.

1190
01:22:11.500 --> 01:22:13.917
No, no... It can't be!

1191
01:22:14.333 --> 01:22:16.250
He can't have done this.

1192
01:22:17.500 --> 01:22:19.792
- Dad...
- I want to make on thing clear.

1193
01:22:20.000 --> 01:22:22.750
Not for a moment did I believe
that you'd found him.

1194
01:22:23.708 --> 01:22:25.042
He was here.

1195
01:22:26.042 --> 01:22:31.500
I look at you and I want to push
the button and send all this to shit!

1196
01:22:34.250 --> 01:22:36.625
You're shame your family.

1197
01:22:37.125 --> 01:22:41.125
At your age, your grandma Ursula
had subjugated a whole galaxy!

1198
01:22:41.458 --> 01:22:43.917
Your cousin Virguis is just 18

1199
01:22:44.125 --> 01:22:47.083
and he's already done
two genocides on Alpha Centauri!

1200
01:22:47.250 --> 01:22:48.833
And look at you!

1201
01:22:49.042 --> 01:22:51.333
How have you let
this planet go on like this?

1202
01:22:51.625 --> 01:22:55.292
Alive! So alive it's disgusting!

1203
01:22:55.667 --> 01:22:59.417
Where's the lava, the chaos!

1204
01:22:59.542 --> 01:23:01.708
I want volcanoes everywhere!

1205
01:23:02.917 --> 01:23:07.500
The whole planet's under my control,
although they don't know it.

1206
01:23:07.667 --> 01:23:09.833
What good is it
if they don't know it?!

1207
01:23:10.542 --> 01:23:12.792
You're like a useless pet, like a...

1208
01:23:13.417 --> 01:23:15.000
I don't know what you are, Agata,

1209
01:23:15.167 --> 01:23:17.833
but I wish you weren't my daughter!

1210
01:23:18.375 --> 01:23:21.250
Where's your mettle
to be leader of Chiton?

1211
01:23:21.417 --> 01:23:23.208
Where's your character?

1212
01:23:23.375 --> 01:23:26.792
Where's your mettle
to do important things?

1213
01:23:28.042 --> 01:23:29.500
Right here.

1214
01:23:45.083 --> 01:23:46.500
<i>At last, my girl.</i>

1215
01:23:47.500 --> 01:23:50.833
<i>Now, yes. I am proud of you.</i>

1216
01:24:10.500 --> 01:24:11.583
Any objections?

1217
01:24:13.250 --> 01:24:17.125
Then move it.
I have a planet to raze.

1218
01:24:21.625 --> 01:24:23.542
- Are you sure?
- Look, Luisa.

1219
01:24:23.708 --> 01:24:25.458
I may have all the superpowers,

1220
01:24:25.583 --> 01:24:27.125
but understanding you
isn't one of them yet.

1221
01:24:27.292 --> 01:24:28.250
- Me?
- Yes, you.

1222
01:24:28.417 --> 01:24:29.417
A few days ago,

1223
01:24:29.542 --> 01:24:31.417
you thought being a superhero
was pathetic.

1224
01:24:31.542 --> 01:24:32.833
Now you won't burn
the suit, just in case.

1225
01:24:33.042 --> 01:24:35.750
Agata will keep looking for you
and you'll need to defend yourself.

1226
01:24:35.917 --> 01:24:38.458
If I stop being a superhero,
maybe she'll stop looking.

1227
01:24:39.292 --> 01:24:41.250
I shouldn't have stopped
that darn subway train.

1228
01:24:41.417 --> 01:24:42.833
- That's when the problems started.
- Oh, really?

1229
01:24:43.042 --> 01:24:45.333
Were you really doing
so great before this?

1230
01:24:46.083 --> 01:24:47.542
Burning the suit
won't make you normal.

1231
01:24:47.708 --> 01:24:49.708
You know what really makes me mad?

1232
01:24:49.875 --> 01:24:52.458
Precisely these days
I couldn't be normal.

1233
01:24:52.792 --> 01:24:54.708
If I had been,
we wouldn't be arguing now.

1234
01:24:54.875 --> 01:24:57.000
Or we'd be arguing over
whether to go out to dinner or not.

1235
01:24:57.167 --> 01:25:00.333
Or if we'd meet up again,
which, by the way, I want to.

1236
01:25:02.417 --> 01:25:04.458
But you can't choose
to be like everyone else

1237
01:25:04.583 --> 01:25:06.042
because you're not like everyone else.

1238
01:25:08.500 --> 01:25:10.792
I can choose. Look.

1239
01:25:17.417 --> 01:25:18.917
Tell them this is going to stick.

1240
01:25:19.125 --> 01:25:20.750
Give them some time,
I know Juan.

1241
01:25:20.917 --> 01:25:24.125
You're his parents,
but I'm his boss and his friend.

1242
01:25:24.292 --> 01:25:27.333
And you're not his parents, parents.
So listen to me.

1243
01:25:29.250 --> 01:25:30.708
I saw this coming!

1244
01:25:30.875 --> 01:25:33.333
- Tell Juanito to hide!
- What are you doing, Juan?

1245
01:25:33.500 --> 01:25:35.208
These scum will see
who his father is!

1246
01:25:35.375 --> 01:25:37.417
When I find the cartridges,
I'll show 'em.

1247
01:25:37.542 --> 01:25:39.417
What's going on here?

1248
01:25:40.500 --> 01:25:41.667
That's going on.

1249
01:25:48.375 --> 01:25:49.708
- It's not burning!
- Yes it is.

1250
01:25:49.875 --> 01:25:51.500
It just needs catch fire.

1251
01:25:51.625 --> 01:25:52.750
Of course it'll burn.

1252
01:25:52.917 --> 01:25:54.792
It wouldn't be the weirdest thing
we've seen lately.

1253
01:25:55.000 --> 01:25:57.542
Now everything that happens here
has to be weird!

1254
01:25:57.708 --> 01:25:59.417
Let's stop being so paranoid.

1255
01:25:59.542 --> 01:26:01.083
Juanito!

1256
01:26:01.250 --> 01:26:04.833
Juanito, look!
The aliens are invading!

1257
01:26:20.333 --> 01:26:22.500
She couldn't be
a bigger pain in the ass.

1258
01:26:22.625 --> 01:26:24.500
What's the suit doing there?

1259
01:26:24.625 --> 01:26:27.167
- I'm not wearing it anymore, Mom!
- Why not?

1260
01:26:27.333 --> 01:26:29.875
It turned out so nice,
and the stitching I had to do!

1261
01:26:30.583 --> 01:26:32.333
How can you be so tiresome?

1262
01:26:32.500 --> 01:26:35.375
Where are going with a UFO
right here in town?

1263
01:26:35.500 --> 01:26:39.250
You must be really dumb.
I don't want any trouble!

1264
01:26:39.417 --> 01:26:42.750
- First of all, good morning.
- I'm not going to your planet!

1265
01:26:42.917 --> 01:26:45.500
- You didn't persuade me!
- I don't have to persuade you.

1266
01:26:45.667 --> 01:26:48.667
I'm going to raze this planet,
starting with your family.

1267
01:26:48.833 --> 01:26:51.583
Now you're razing the planet.
With what, a giant toaster?

1268
01:26:51.750 --> 01:26:53.667
Have you looked at yourself?

1269
01:27:20.500 --> 01:27:21.917
The suit!

1270
01:27:22.125 --> 01:27:23.833
- The suit!
- The suit!

1271
01:27:25.708 --> 01:27:27.167
- Come on.
- The stick!

1272
01:27:30.625 --> 01:27:31.625
- Be careful.
- Here, Juan.

1273
01:27:31.792 --> 01:27:32.792
- Come on!
- Come here.

1274
01:27:33.000 --> 01:27:35.042
- Tell me you're not scared.
- I'm not scared!

1275
01:27:35.208 --> 01:27:36.042
Even you don't believe that.

1276
01:27:36.208 --> 01:27:38.875
Jaime, if she tells me not
to be scared, I say I'm not.

1277
01:27:39.083 --> 01:27:40.875
But sure I'm scared.
Look at that monstrosity!

1278
01:27:41.083 --> 01:27:44.500
- Two days in the same underpants!
- It keeps growing!

1279
01:27:46.250 --> 01:27:46.917
Come on.

1280
01:27:47.792 --> 01:27:49.375
- It's hot, it's hot!
- Alright...

1281
01:27:49.500 --> 01:27:52.000
Put a foot in here, in here!

1282
01:27:57.125 --> 01:28:00.042
If my mom helps me put on
the suit, I'll never have charisma.

1283
01:28:00.208 --> 01:28:01.833
It's almost on us, Juan!

1284
01:28:04.542 --> 01:28:05.708
Go!

1285
01:28:08.667 --> 01:28:09.708
Leave me alone with her!

1286
01:28:09.875 --> 01:28:11.667
- How can we go?
- Get out of here!

1287
01:28:11.833 --> 01:28:14.167
Go! Go!

1288
01:28:24.500 --> 01:28:26.000
What?

1289
01:28:26.250 --> 01:28:27.750
Whatever you say, he's my son.

1290
01:28:31.500 --> 01:28:33.208
By the Great Hornspoon!

1291
01:28:33.917 --> 01:28:35.333
Leave my family alone!

1292
01:28:35.667 --> 01:28:38.500
- This is between you and me!
- Family...

1293
01:28:38.667 --> 01:28:40.500
Family is overrated.

1294
01:28:50.292 --> 01:28:51.583
My shotgun!

1295
01:28:56.500 --> 01:28:58.500
- Hold on, Dad!
- I can't, son!

1296
01:28:58.625 --> 01:29:00.042
It looks like I can't!

1297
01:29:00.500 --> 01:29:02.708
Hold on, Juan! Hold on!

1298
01:29:06.875 --> 01:29:08.500
I'm sorry.

1299
01:29:08.667 --> 01:29:11.833
- I think it's time to stand out!
- Of course, son!

1300
01:29:12.042 --> 01:29:14.458
Show the universe
what the Lopezes are worth!

1301
01:29:18.333 --> 01:29:19.333
Dad!

1302
01:29:22.292 --> 01:29:26.167
Relax, son!
I've got it all under control!

1303
01:29:27.375 --> 01:29:28.375
He's been sucked up!

1304
01:29:42.875 --> 01:29:45.375
- Isn't that the loser?
- Be quiet.

1305
01:29:56.417 --> 01:29:59.583
This is going straight to YouTube.
Transformer vs. Sissy.

1306
01:30:02.708 --> 01:30:05.292
She's going to kill him!

1307
01:30:06.625 --> 01:30:08.375
Juanito!

1308
01:30:12.917 --> 01:30:14.167
Here she comes...

1309
01:30:18.792 --> 01:30:21.292
<i>Look out, danger.
The ball on the right side.</i>

1310
01:30:21.458 --> 01:30:23.167
<i>It'll reach Leo Messi, Leo...</i>

1311
01:30:23.333 --> 01:30:25.208
<i>Ball to the goalie, but look out,
there's a field-crasher.</i>

1312
01:30:25.375 --> 01:30:26.250
Who's that?

1313
01:30:26.417 --> 01:30:29.917
<i>Someone's down on the pitch,
but not a player, a field-crasher.</i>

1314
01:30:30.125 --> 01:30:32.833
What a shitty field-crasher!

1315
01:30:33.042 --> 01:30:35.167
He's not even naked!

1316
01:30:35.500 --> 01:30:37.583
<i>He confronts the referee
and tells him it's a penalty.</i>

1317
01:30:37.750 --> 01:30:39.375
<i>We can't believe it.</i>

1318
01:30:41.292 --> 01:30:43.125
<i>What's this guy doing?
Get him off the field!</i>

1319
01:30:43.292 --> 01:30:45.708
Throw him off the field, ref!

1320
01:30:45.875 --> 01:30:48.125
He's going to fuck up the final.

1321
01:30:48.292 --> 01:30:49.792
<i>It's incredible.
Look at the players' faces.</i>

1322
01:30:50.000 --> 01:30:52.833
<i>He's grabbing the net.
Someone get this guy off!</i>

1323
01:31:02.667 --> 01:31:04.375
Guys, look.

1324
01:31:28.375 --> 01:31:30.667
- What are you doing here?
- Don't ask.

1325
01:31:34.167 --> 01:31:37.417
- What have you done with my parents?
- I told you, they're not your parents.

1326
01:31:48.000 --> 01:31:49.375
No, no, no!

1327
01:31:56.500 --> 01:31:57.375
Jaime.

1328
01:31:58.583 --> 01:32:00.333
Jaime, help me.
You have to distract her.

1329
01:32:00.500 --> 01:32:02.125
I'm sorry, the robot?

1330
01:32:02.292 --> 01:32:04.000
- You're crazy.
- She's going to destroy him!

1331
01:32:04.167 --> 01:32:06.250
- But we can't do anything.
- Of course we can!

1332
01:32:06.417 --> 01:32:09.208
- Distract her somehow!
- Wait, wait.

1333
01:32:09.875 --> 01:32:11.167
I have a better man.

1334
01:32:11.333 --> 01:32:14.417
You and I go down to the basement
and stay there a couple of days.

1335
01:32:14.542 --> 01:32:17.375
What? Are you trying
something with me, Jaime?

1336
01:32:17.875 --> 01:32:19.333
But I was very subtle.

1337
01:32:22.583 --> 01:32:24.500
Shit, shit! Shit!

1338
01:32:25.125 --> 01:32:27.333
This is the famous ultimate weapon.

1339
01:32:27.500 --> 01:32:31.583
Okay. I'd keep playing,
but I have a planet to destroy.

1340
01:32:39.250 --> 01:32:40.333
Hey, Agata!

1341
01:32:41.083 --> 01:32:43.625
Here, read my mind!

1342
01:32:43.792 --> 01:32:47.125
I'm thinking you should follow me!

1343
01:32:53.750 --> 01:32:55.417
- Grab something.
- It's too soft in here.

1344
01:32:55.542 --> 01:32:56.875
- Up!
- I can't, Juan.

1345
01:32:57.083 --> 01:32:58.417
Up!

1346
01:33:00.833 --> 01:33:02.500
I almost distracted her.

1347
01:33:02.708 --> 01:33:05.083
- What...?
- Juan, you're useless!

1348
01:33:05.250 --> 01:33:06.500
Piece of shit!

1349
01:33:06.625 --> 01:33:09.292
Hey, insult my son again
and you're screwed!

1350
01:33:09.833 --> 01:33:12.333
I know it sounds weird,
but it works.

1351
01:33:12.500 --> 01:33:15.625
Juan, you're ugly! Real ugly!

1352
01:33:16.083 --> 01:33:18.833
We all pull together
or the planet's screwed!

1353
01:33:27.500 --> 01:33:28.333
Juan!

1354
01:33:29.000 --> 01:33:30.375
Juan!

1355
01:33:31.500 --> 01:33:32.917
Juan, get up!

1356
01:33:38.750 --> 01:33:42.833
Juanito, an adopted child
isn't loved like a real one.

1357
01:33:43.042 --> 01:33:46.500
- You're getting beaten by a girl!
- Get up, Juan!

1358
01:33:46.667 --> 01:33:50.292
Help! Wake up!

1359
01:33:55.458 --> 01:33:56.500
Juan, I'm here!

1360
01:34:31.542 --> 01:34:35.292
- Fine. Let's end this.
- I agree!

1361
01:34:54.458 --> 01:34:55.917
Like on our first date, Juan!

1362
01:34:58.042 --> 01:35:00.208
Blow her down in one!

1363
01:35:06.708 --> 01:35:07.750
My mother!

1364
01:35:09.083 --> 01:35:13.208
Luisa grabbed my ass a while ago!
Your mom's grabbing it now!

1365
01:35:39.708 --> 01:35:42.625
- I can blow you down in one.
- Don't play the hero, Lopez.

1366
01:35:42.792 --> 01:35:43.917
It's not your thing.

1367
01:35:44.667 --> 01:35:46.500
My name is Superlopez.

1368
01:36:15.792 --> 01:36:19.667
- Did he say Superlopez?
- I liked Sissy more.

1369
01:36:22.375 --> 01:36:23.792
- Help!
- Juan...

1370
01:36:24.000 --> 01:36:24.833
Are you alright?

1371
01:36:25.042 --> 01:36:26.792
Get me out of here!

1372
01:36:29.708 --> 01:36:31.083
- Are you alright?
- No, I'm not.

1373
01:36:31.250 --> 01:36:32.167
- That's it.
- How awful.

1374
01:36:32.333 --> 01:36:35.083
You're welcome, Juanito.
Second time I've saved you.

1375
01:36:35.667 --> 01:36:36.375
- Son.
- Son.

1376
01:36:36.500 --> 01:36:37.708
I almost got killed!

1377
01:36:39.542 --> 01:36:42.208
Son, your father almost drowned.

1378
01:36:42.375 --> 01:36:43.417
It was terrible.

1379
01:36:43.542 --> 01:36:45.208
It's alright.

1380
01:36:45.375 --> 01:36:47.208
You've left me with no hats.

1381
01:36:55.708 --> 01:36:56.750
Well...

1382
01:36:56.917 --> 01:36:59.250
You saw what I did, right!?

1383
01:36:59.417 --> 01:37:01.375
Maybe you are
a bit of a superhero.

1384
01:37:02.292 --> 01:37:05.292
Maybe, yes.
What do we do now?

1385
01:37:06.583 --> 01:37:11.042
- And landing in that pose.
- Yes, it wasn't on purpose.

1386
01:37:11.208 --> 01:37:13.583
I don't know if
you'll get used to it.

1387
01:37:14.667 --> 01:37:15.500
What choice is there?

1388
01:37:15.667 --> 01:37:18.208
Just thinking about it
gives me a knot in my gullet.

1389
01:37:18.375 --> 01:37:22.500
But your real parents on Chiton
are waiting for you to save them.

1390
01:37:23.208 --> 01:37:24.083
Don't worry, Mom.

1391
01:37:25.917 --> 01:37:27.417
I've got it all under control.

1392
01:37:43.417 --> 01:37:46.000
<i>My son, it's been so long.</i>

1393
01:37:46.167 --> 01:37:47.917
Thanks to you, son,

1394
01:37:48.125 --> 01:37:51.667
Chiton will finally be a free planet.

1395
01:37:51.833 --> 01:37:54.792
Son, we've missed you so much.

1396
01:37:55.375 --> 01:37:57.125
We knew you'd come back!

1397
01:38:06.333 --> 01:38:09.000
Come, son. Give me a kiss.

1398
01:38:19.333 --> 01:38:20.833
PLANET: CHITON
LEADER: ADMIRAL SKORBA

1399
01:38:21.750 --> 01:38:24.000
LEADER: JEFERSON NORUEGA

1400
01:39:29.875 --> 01:39:31.458
<i>Good morning. We awake today</i>

1401
01:39:31.583 --> 01:39:34.375
<i>with the news of the emergence
of this strange superhero.</i>

1402
01:39:34.500 --> 01:39:36.833
<i>Images of him have gone viral.</i>

1403
01:39:37.042 --> 01:39:39.500
<i>City Hall is raising taxes</i>

1404
01:39:39.625 --> 01:39:42.000
<i>to pay for the destruction
in the city.</i>

1405
01:39:42.167 --> 01:39:44.500
<i>And we have to add
another headaches to this.</i>

1406
01:39:44.667 --> 01:39:49.208
<i>Indeed, there's the stoppage
on Line 1 due to the accident</i>

1407
01:39:49.375 --> 01:39:53.625
<i>and protests by fans
at the suspension of the Cup Final.</i>

1408
01:39:53.792 --> 01:39:56.917
<i>Lots of listener messages
on our answering machine.</i>

1409
01:39:57.417 --> 01:40:02.000
<i>This country, Spain,
has had real superheroes,</i>

1410
01:40:02.167 --> 01:40:04.792
<i>like Don Pelayo, like El Cid,</i>

1411
01:40:05.000 --> 01:40:08.167
<i>we don't deserve some guy
flying around in a leotard.</i>

1412
01:40:08.708 --> 01:40:12.458
<i>I think this superhero
is a smokescreen</i>

1413
01:40:12.583 --> 01:40:15.042
<i>so we don't talk about
what really matters.</i>

1414
01:40:15.375 --> 01:40:19.167
<i>I'm 86, a widow for 40 years.</i>

1415
01:40:19.333 --> 01:40:21.167
<i>I've fantasized about making love</i>

1416
01:40:21.333 --> 01:40:24.083
<i>to all the superheroes
in alphabetical order.</i>

1417
01:40:24.250 --> 01:40:26.833
<i>Can you believe that
this Spanish superhero</i>

1418
01:40:27.042 --> 01:40:28.750
<i>arouses no desire in me?</i>

1419
01:40:28.917 --> 01:40:32.083
<i>He looks so skinny,
so scrawny, so ugly,</i>

1420
01:40:32.250 --> 01:40:36.625
<i>with that ridiculous name...
What is it? What's he called?</i>

1421
01:40:56.833 --> 01:40:57.500
Don't start.

1422
01:40:57.667 --> 01:41:00.458
- You always do this to me, Juan!
- What do you want me to do?

1423
01:41:00.917 --> 01:41:04.458
I saw a column of smoke
and my body said: save humanity.

1424
01:41:04.583 --> 01:41:05.917
Now it's fires too.

1425
01:41:06.125 --> 01:41:08.792
When it's not a fire, it's a robbery,
or that boat the other day.

1426
01:41:09.000 --> 01:41:10.833
Luisa, it was a cruise ship
and it was sinking.

1427
01:41:11.042 --> 01:41:14.292
Sorry, whatever. Now it's smoke!
There are firemen!

1428
01:41:14.458 --> 01:41:17.375
When I see someone
in imminent danger,

1429
01:41:17.500 --> 01:41:21.125
naturally I save them.
If I don't, I think that's terrible.

1430
01:41:21.292 --> 01:41:22.917
So what do I have to do
to get you to come on time?

1431
01:41:23.125 --> 01:41:24.292
Set fire to the restaurant?

1432
01:41:24.458 --> 01:41:25.750
I've been late twice.

1433
01:41:25.917 --> 01:41:27.542
15 minutes to save the planet
and look how you get.

1434
01:41:27.708 --> 01:41:30.000
Look, Juan, I'll tell you.
As of now,

1435
01:41:30.167 --> 01:41:31.333
you're going to have to combine

1436
01:41:31.500 --> 01:41:33.292
your superhero life
with life in a couple.

1437
01:41:33.458 --> 01:41:37.375
I'll tell you: if there's
a catastrophe and I do nothing,

1438
01:41:38.125 --> 01:41:39.083
it's your fault!

1439
01:41:41.375 --> 01:41:43.167
- Fine.
- Fine.

1440
01:41:44.500 --> 01:41:45.583
Get the bill, go on.

1441
01:41:50.500 --> 01:41:54.333
- Waiter, check, please.
- The man at the bar is buying.

1442
01:42:06.167 --> 01:42:08.917
You owe me one, Superlopez.

